{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant","id":1350432,"title":"Is you Dynast PC evil or merely ignorant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-23T06:44:05-08:00","id":1350432,"title":"Is you Dynast PC evil or merely ignorant?","content":"<b>***HETERODOX VIEWS FOLLOW***YOU HAVE BEEN WARNED***</b><br /> <br /> I'm asking about a PC that you're actually playing rather than one that you theoretically might play or used to play (in an attempt to avoid the NIMBY problem).<br /> <br /> Given that the Realm is a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating murder machine of unreasoning cruelty and injustice without many if any redeeming features, is your current Dynast PC a champion of this evil empire (and thus evil herself) or completely ignorant of it (and thus painfully blind)? Does your PC stand against the Realm? Some other relationship?<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how people play Dynasts as heroic characters. (If your Dynast is herself a corrupt monster, then no need to explain since that's easy to see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T07:32:49-08:00","id":1350438,"title":"","content":"My DB PC killed a Delhzan woman in cold blood because in her 20 years of being a spoilt Cynis scion, she was the first mortal who ever told her &quot;No&quot; to something she asked, and didn't know how to act except by imposing her authority.<br /> <br /> I would like to think she was being misguided, but well, it's pretty hard to not see her as evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T07:44:54-08:00","id":1350439,"title":"","content":"Mostly ignorant.<br /> <br /> Most of my Dynastic Dragon-Blooded PCs were fairly young and the majority of their adult life has been during the Time of Tumult where there's this gigantic Anathema resurgence that a lot of Storytellers really struggle to avoid due to it being such a focus of the gameline and an obvious way to challenge 3-5 Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> So when the rebellious Satrapy really is the work of a shapeshifting terrorist whose murdered and replaced their way into a position of power it's hard to really reflect on the evils of empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T09:02:22-08:00","id":1350447,"title":"","content":"Is this only PCs or do NPC portrayals by a ST count?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T09:16:40-08:00","id":1350449,"title":"","content":"Does &quot;so blinded by fervor and loyalty to Mnemon they actively refuse to engage but is a noble person otherwise&quot; count as ignorant?<br /> <br /> Because that's my Prasadi Pasiap graduate character is like; he literally cannot let himself believe that Mnemon is anything less than the noble, destined heir to the throne. He'd blanch at the Wyld Hunt at its worst, but he's her hand, body and soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T09:25:05-08:00","id":1350451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant#post1350432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>***HETERODOX VIEWS FOLLOW***YOU HAVE BEEN WARNED***</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really feel I have been; you say your own views will follow, but then ask how other people play things in their games. So which one is the thread about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T10:21:14-08:00","id":1350456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant#post1350432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>***HETERODOX VIEWS FOLLOW***YOU HAVE BEEN WARNED***</b><br /> <br /> Given that the Realm is a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating murder machine of unreasoning cruelty and injustice without many if any redeeming features</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unsure I read the same book than you. It that's not the case, you should try to read The Realm book. I don't think your description is accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T10:31:41-08:00","id":1350460,"title":"","content":"Yeah, how storytellers and players themselves view the Realm varies. As someone who doesn't accept the thesis statement here (or rather, argues that if true the Realm is being portrayed incorrectly) my PoV as a Dynast player doesn't really feel relevant. Which makes this a weird discussion as it's trying to seek different perspectives?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T10:48:21-08:00","id":1350464,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not currently running a Dragon-Blooded PC, but I don\u2019t think the Realm is as bad as you say it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T13:09:16-08:00","id":1350499,"title":"","content":"Hyperbole?<br /> <br /> I mean, the Realm is not a &quot;baby-eating machine&quot;. But it is a parasitic empire, and the Dragonblood are the ones in charge of it. It's still a fair point, if we take a simple and straightforward view of whether the people in the ruling class of an evil empire are evil (which of course, not everyone would agree with).<br /> <br /> Of course, almost every Dragonblood<i> is</i> ignorant or evil+ignorant (again, taking the straightforward view that the ruling class of an evil empire are all evil), because the Immaculate Philosophy is designed to make them ignorant; not as ignorant as peasants (many do know that the Solars and Lunars actually are just humans who are Exalted like them, whereas most peasants think the Anathema are literal demons), but it is designed to make them believe that Solars and Lunars will inevitably become dangerous, mad and evil, and so there is no choice but to kill them. There aren't really many Dragonblood who realise the Realm's guiding philosophy is just propaganda made up to stop the Solars, and decide not to kill them. (There are probably some who realise it's propaganda, and decide to kill Solars and Lunars anyway).<br /> <br /> But not all. And if you read Equitable Remedy's whole post, they do ask about how people play Dragonblood heroically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-23-2019, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T13:14:16-08:00","id":1350501,"title":"","content":"Sadly, Equitable Remedy said PCs that are played now, so I can't answer this question. I've played 5 or 6 Dynast PCs, but they were all a long time ago, we overplayed Dragonblood games and so stopped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T13:29:38-08:00","id":1350505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350499#post1350499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But not all. And if you read Equitable Remedy's whole post, they do ask about how people play Lunars heroically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err.... I've reread the OP a few times Wiz, and I can't find any mention of Lunars in the OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T13:39:39-08:00","id":1350510,"title":"","content":"Well, I'll try and give my take, since I do have a Dynast character in play, sort of<br /> <br /> Tepet Forivas isn't respected. The phrase 'barely a Dynast' comes up a lot with him. Legally he's a full member of the dynasty - his mother was a Tepet, he inherits through her. That said his mother was informally exiled to a far northern fishing village as Tepet's mercantile ambassador to the region. She was <b>disgraced </b>and it wasn't seriously thought she'd bare offspring of account. Even Forivas Exalting wasn't enough to get him accepted. But post Futile Blood Tepet are a lot less picky about their family members.<br /> <br /> Forivas isn't blind, and he's far from unsympathetic to the issues the Realm's governance causes. He's got little personal love for snooty dynasts who look down their noses at his pedigree or upbringing, which is pretty much every island born Dynast he's ever met. However, he's ultimately in favour of the Realm as a <i>concept</i>, regardless of the specific issues defending it can cause. He sees reports time and time again of Lunar attacks, cities falling to plague, rioting or civil war. When there's chaos and misrule on seemingly every front, the status quo becomes appealing. Rule through strength, a focus on order and control. Anyone wanting to challenge the Realm comes off as self serving to him - out for personal power, and heedless of the consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T14:11:07-08:00","id":1350513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350505#post1350505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Err.... I've reread the OP a few times Wiz, and I can't find any mention of Lunars in the OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Sorry, that was a typo. I meant Dragonblood. Probably I've been talking about my Lunar game to my friends too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T14:30:32-08:00","id":1350516,"title":"","content":"I am not running or playing in a DB game, so I cannot answer the question you literally asked. Having said that, I think that even under the assumption that Realm is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant#post1350432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating murder machine of unreasoning cruelty and injustice without many if any redeeming features</div> </div> </div> </div>the dichotomy doesn't really hold. <br /> <br /> I have some small background and hold some interest in history and even a little bit of exposure make you realise how extremely different mental frameworks can people have. Very often reactions, opinions or deeds of people in not so distant eras can strike one not even as bad, but rather as completely alien. And at some point, you realise that your default network of emotional reactions is really to a large extent determined by your culture - a trivial observation, not so trivial anymore, once you realise this is true and when you realise that there is 99 percent chance that some people in the future will consider your views outrageous for reasons you would never guess. This doesn't mean that they will be wrong or that there is nothing objective to it, but possibly that fixing your ethical worldview is a hard philosophical endevour.<br /> <br /> Now, when I run or play games in quasi-historical settings (as in, vaguely related to historic cultures), I really like to treat that idea seriously and make default reactions of surrounding people genuinely alien - they can desperately desire or vehemently despise things in a manner that we cannot really follow emotionally, but whose general logic we can understand based on some general knowledge. <br /> <br /> Now, I really like this feeling of slight detachment between the player and the character, when they behave in a way deeply embedded in non-contemporary world-views. I find it similar to the dramatic irony when the player knowledge could prevent characters from taking some action, but we all indulge following the internal logic of the story. <br /> <br /> So, according to your classification, I think I would play or encourage players to play Dragon-Blooded characters which could be called &quot;painfully blind&quot;, but I think it's better to just take them as embedded in their own culture. Of course there is some space for reformer characters that try to change their societies - but I really to avoid overt anachronisms in depicting people's mentalities. The characters are not blind (or, they are, but this is visible only to us). They only have really different standards of what is a normal behaviour.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T00:08:57-08:00","id":1350593,"title":"","content":"As a British group of players, we tend to play Dragonblood as Imperial-era British aristocrats; they may be brave, they may be willing to endure hardship for the sake of King and Country, they may want to help poorer countries (&quot;may&quot; being the operative word), but much of their efforts are deeply tainted and twisted by prejudice. Even the well-meaning ones firmly believe that a strong empire of Dragonblood is best for everyone, that the Realm's culture and religion are best, that peasants are stupid, that all Anathema must die.<br /> <br /> Is that evil or ignorant? Is someone who believes bad is good evil or ignorant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T00:32:16-08:00","id":1350597,"title":"","content":"I'm among those rejecting the premise. <br /> I feel that any line of thought that begins with &quot;If you are a ____, you are either evil or ignorant.&quot; is an extremely dangerous line of thought that has no business being entertained because it is dehumanization of the opposition and us-versus-them thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T01:23:22-08:00","id":1350601,"title":"","content":"Eh, well it depends. &quot;If you are a murderer, you are either evil or ignorant,&quot; is something many might not disagree with. Though I imagine most would add &quot;pushed by desperate circumstances.&quot; And there's an argument that the Dragonblood's attempt to wipe out all Solars and Lunars comes under that category.<br /> <br /> Now, I think the OP's claim that Dynasts are evil or ignorant is very<i> simplistic</i>, as evil is not a binary state. People can be evil in some ways and good in others. And, you know, your common murderer isn't as evil as the architects of genocide. And even Gandhi and Mother Teresa did some things that look kind of dubious. Evil's less yes/no, and more of a spectrum.<br /> <br /> But I think again, the OP's over-use of hyperbole* has distracted from their final sentence, asking for examples of heroic Dragonblood. So if you think Dragonblood dynasts don't have to be evil, show examples from current games.<br /> <br /> For example, my friend's character Mnemon Ysselda is an abolitionist who fights for the rights of peasants and tries to get the Realm to follow a more ethical foreign policy. She can be a bit of a champagne socialist at times, and there are arguments that her methods aren't effective, but she's trying.<br /> <br /> *I mean, I'm being charitable here. I'm assuming it's hyperbole to attract attention to this thread. Obviously the Realm is not a society where people literally eat babies, that's one of their enemies.**<br /> <br /> **And a strong reason why people might support the Realm. It's better than Rakshi. Like 40k; yes, the Imperium is awful, but their enemies are worse. Or, you know, some of our real life governments. I had a student from Syria who supported Assad. He didn't like him, but as Christian from a Christian village he considered Al-Nusra and the other groups Assad was fighting to be worse.<br /> I think Croakamancer showed a good example of a Dynast whose justification is this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-24-2019, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T02:16:59-08:00","id":1350605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350601#post1350601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think again, the OP's over-use of hyperbole* has distracted from their final sentence, asking for examples of heroic Dragonblood. So if you think Dragonblood dynasts don't have to be evil, show examples from current games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the flashing title got the attention of many people indeed. What I disagree in this presentation is that it suggests you can't support the Realm policy and be a hero\u00efc character, which I think makes the beauty and subtility of Exalted world poorer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T02:23:49-08:00","id":1350607,"title":"","content":"I think every Exalted character I've ever played is both evil and ignorant. They've (mostly) been human after all.<br /> <br /> The Realm has prevented the total destruction of all Creation. Every Lunar and Solar fighting against the Realm is fighting for the destruction of Creation.<br /> <br /> Every Sidereal, Gold or Bronze, sees only part of Fate which itself is only part of what makes reality tick.<br /> <br /> Are the police officers who work in your city evil or ignorant? I can absolutely guarentee that whatever country you're in, you have at least one unjust law and one criminal those police officers haven't stopped. I can also guarentee your local cops haven't led a perfect life without sin.<br /> <br /> But chances are (most of) your local cops are doing the best they can with the society they were born into. Yes, the government is funding terrorists to overthrow middle eastern states, and yes they're also selling the weapons being used to commit genocide in Yemen. But your local beat cops are putting their lives on the line, walking the streets to stop murderers and rapists.<br /> <br /> Same for your Dynasts. They're part of a system. That system objectively has aspects which are not good. But it also has parts which are good -- like stopping armies of cannibals descending on the Satrapies and eating everyone. And what you play is your choice. You can be the heroic beat-cop, helping Old Man McClusty cross the road and rushing into danger to free girls from sex trafficing. Or you can be a racist, abusive, powermad ass.<br /> <br /> But there's nothing inherent to being a Dynast that makes them evil or ignorant compared to any other PC. The Bull of the North rules a tribe of murderous barbarians. The Queen of Fangs <i>literally</i> eats babies.<br /> <br /> You don't play The Realm. You play a Dynast.<br /> <br /> My 3E Dynast character, Cynis Ganan, is a pretty bad example. He's deliberately evil and ignorant. But he's not without redeeming features. He's a hero in the classical sense, a champion who selflessly throws himself into danger to protect others. He loves his children. He wants to provide genuine guidance for mortals on how to improve their lives. He's not deliberately cruel to people or animals. He (basically) never lies. He's brave. He puts his wife's happiness before his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-24-2019, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T02:46:41-08:00","id":1350614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350607#post1350607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think every Exalted character I've ever played is both evil and ignorant. They've (mostly) been human after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Bull of the North rules a tribe of murderous barbarians. The Queen of Fangs <i>literally</i> eats babies. </div> </div> </div>The Dragonblood games I've played generally featured a bunch of decadent paternalist bigoted aristos.<br /> <br /> The Dawn in the Solar game I play is worse than nearly all of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But chances are (most of) your local cops are doing the best they can with the society they were born into. Yes, the government is funding terrorists to overthrow middle eastern states, and yes they're also selling the weapons being used to commit genocide in Yemen. But your local beat cops are putting their lives on the line, walking the streets to stop murderers and rapists. </div> </div> </div>So I was thinking earlier, while reading this thread, about the Realm's magistrates. Heroes of the peasantry, rooting out corruption, punishing even wicked Dynasts.<br /> Of course, they're also not really dealing with the core issues of the Dynasty, just papering over the cracks. But... someone does need to do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there's nothing inherent to being a Dynast that makes them evil or ignorant compared to any other PC. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... while I kind of agree with your overall point, I don't want to take it too far. There's nothing inherent to being a Dynast that makes them definitely evil. There's a lot of things that push them to be evil.<br /> Which is true for other PCs, but most characters' backgrounds push them towards evil less than being the ruling elite of an expansionist empire and being the objects of veneration for a religion that tells them they're better than others.<br /> <br /> I mean, if we take say...<br /> Cynis Kuran, who grew up surrounded by wealth and luxury and slaves who he was encouraged to use for whatever he liked, and to whom peasants bow down and do whatever he says, and who was constantly told he was better than most people, and that his country was better than other countries because the people in those countries are evil and backward. His parents, who he was told to emulate, were slave traders and blackmailers.<br /> Humble Ox, a peasant from a poor farming village who grew up seeing her parents mistreated by those more powerful than him.<br /> <br /> Both can be good. Both can be evil. They have free will. Both, when put in difficult moral situations, may screw up. Maybe Kuran is disgusted by what he sees and decides to put things to rights. Maybe Humble Ox decides she's going to make it big, whatever it takes, and becomes a gangster, to ensure she's the one doing the mistreatment. But I think Cynis Kuran is much more<i> likely</i> to be evil (or... well, higher up the evil scale, because again it's not simply binary).<br /> <br /> I'm not really trying to disagree with your point, because you're right, a Dynast doesn't <i>have</i> to be evil. They don't have an &quot;evil gene&quot;. I just don't want to swing so far that we start saying it does not at all matter whether you've been raised to rule a parasitic empire or not. Overall, Dragonblood Dynasts are probably worse people than average (and mortal Dynasts are probably even worse).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My 3E Dynast character, Cynis Ganan, is a pretty bad example. He's deliberately evil and ignorant. But he's not without redeeming features. He's a hero in the classical sense, a champion who selflessly throws himself into danger to protect others. He loves his children. He wants to provide genuine guidance for mortals on how to improve their lives. He's not deliberately cruel to people or animals. He (basically) never lies. He's brave. </div> </div> </div>This is a lot more interesting to me than &quot;evil&quot; or &quot;good&quot; characters. No-one's perfect, no-one's 100% evil. And looking at the different ways people in different societies and circumstances characterise evil and good is very interesting (and useful, as it makes you consider what really is &quot;good&quot;, how can people in an imperfect society improve it and be good, etc).<br /> I don't want to therefore get into &quot;oh, good and evil are just subjective&quot; or something, but then, this is a game, and roleplaying games are useful for exploring these things.<br /> (Although they are also supposed to be fun; one of my players was complaining the other day that sometimes people are too interested in exploring, say, playing bigoted anti-heroes, and it gets grating.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and yes they're also selling the weapons being used to commit genocide in Yemen. </div> </div> </div>I'll have you know, thanks to the efforts of one of my local MPs, we officially no longer do this.<br /> <br /> I mean, Bojo's government &quot;forgot&quot; to stop selling the Saudis useful non-weapon systems, like air conditioners for Saudi tanks so they can keep fighting for longer (this is a joke. As if the Saudi army would do any real fighting!) But they said sorry for forgetting! Nor do they put any effort into stopping others selling the Saudis and UAE weapons (the UAE are actually worse than the Saudis, because their proxies are more vicious and torture-happy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-24-2019, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T02:52:41-08:00","id":1350615,"title":"","content":"I think there's a degree of 'should be' in this argument. Like, to be fair to OP, his question makes a lot more sense if you ignore/downplay the even potentially redeeming aspects of the Realm... which I feel Ex3 has done. MoEP Dragon Blooded opens with the story of a Dynast fighting back cannibals and defending mortal troops at the risk of her own life. WFHW opens with a Wyld Hunt willing to put villages to the sword, and The Realm opens with banditry on the Blessed Isle itself. I can't recall offhand any examples of the Ex3 Realm doing stuff that's even marginally benevolent. Immaculate Order aid is focused on 'you should obey the Realm' more, Satrapy status is focused on 'what stuff can we take from you'. There's a feeling of less nurance to me, of less room to defend/support the Realm without being ignorant or malicious. <br /> <br /> Which to me undercuts some of Exalted's central themes. It's hard to question 'would the Solars be better' when the Realm is both crumbling and malevolent. <br /> <br /> (My PoV on where the scale of ambiguity for Exalted should be: if you put Chejop Kejak and Ayesha into a room and had them argue Bronze vs Gold as relevant to the current time period in game, neither should feel clearly right or wrong. Ayesha's got all the issues, all the problems of a Realm that's both crumbling and corrupt. Chejop has a combination of the risk Solars impose, and enough stability in the Realm to make it a credible alternative, if not a good one. Hope vs certainty. That should by its nature be an unwinnable argument, falling to personal preference.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T05:27:08-08:00","id":1350623,"title":"","content":"While there's a fair bit of needlessly provocative hyperbole in the OP, not sure there's a lot of value at this stage in debating *too* much the merits of 3e's portrayal of the Realm relative to past editions.<br /> <br /> Back at the start of 3e I would have said there was a lot of value in talking about it as you could arguably talk about the merits of whether 3e's core was, in the form of the Realm, oversimplifying empires and their historical processes, motivations and the nature and scale of their economics, in favour of pushing a &quot;Fighting imperialism / the Realm and feeling a non-conflicted sense of good about it!&quot; model of Solar games more than in previous editions. Because by being part of that conversation, at least in theory, you could potentially influence the further writing that could substantially moderate or shift the direction established in the core.<br /> <br /> I think after you've got WFHW and FATG written, there seems a bit less purpose!<br /> <br /> Talking about actually realized characters that deal in being interesting within 3e's version of the Realm, as it is, whatever that may be, seems like it could a bit more useful to me? By all means everyone talk about what they want to, and I may be wrong, it is just that going diametrically against what 3e is a bit of a rabbit hole that can ultimately feel a bit futile and dispriting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T06:10:23-08:00","id":1350630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350615#post1350615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm opens with banditry on the Blessed Isle itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I didn't see that as a sign the Realm was bad, so much that the Realm was good, but now it's falling apart. Before, the government kept the peasants safe from bandits. Now the ruler has vanished, the local nobles are squabbling, the centre cannot hold, and banditry rises.<br /> <br /> I mean, in the rest of the world there's plenty of banditry. It's just normal. The Blessed Isle is somewhere where banditry is unusual.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which to me undercuts some of Exalted's central themes. It's hard to question 'would the Solars be better' when the Realm is both crumbling and malevolent.<br /> (My PoV on where the scale of ambiguity for Exalted should be: if you put Chejop Kejak and Ayesha into a room and had them argue Bronze vs Gold as relevant to the current time period in game, neither should feel clearly right or wrong. Ayesha's got all the issues, all the problems of a Realm that's both crumbling and corrupt. Chejop has a combination of the risk Solars impose, and enough stability in the Realm to make it a credible alternative, if not a good one. Hope vs certainty. That should by its nature be an unwinnable argument, falling to personal preference.) </div> </div> </div>So I agree with you about &quot;who should be in charge, Dragonblood or Solars&quot; being something that there shouldn't definitely be an answer to. (I mean, I'd personally argue both are getting stuck in a certain view of the world, but that applies to both so it's fine).<br /> <br /> But I think a crumbling and malevolent Realm is still something you can argue about, because maybe the Solars are <i>worse</i>. Any northern town threatened by the armies of the Bull of the North is not going to go &quot;oh yes, everything would be better under Yurgen Kaneko and his barbarian horde of fanatics.&quot; I'll be honest, your average Dynastic Dragonblood is probably a better person than the Dawn PC I play alongside.<br /> <br /> If the Realm was nice, and efficient, then you wouldn't be able to answer this question because the Bronze Faction is right and the Gold is wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tbh, I kind of think this is Hatewheel's fault. He said that the 2nd ed stuff about the Realm was imperialist apologia, and he wanted to show much more clearly that the Realm is a parasitic empire built on lies and exploitation. A lot of people were like &quot;Woah! Not sure I like this new approach!&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, he liked to portray the Solars as heroes, and talked on forums about this. Yet the game's fluff still has the Bull of the North (even if Lyta and Havesh are no longer mentioned). It still gives them primary allies whose powers are based on cannibalism and who are even more devoted than in 2nd edition to taking peaceful societies and turning them into weapons for a millenia-long war against the Realm.<br /> <br /> And then when the Realm came out (which was not written by Hatewheel or Holden), it showed a country that, well, was actually one of the nicer places to live in Creation, even if it does have exploitative nobles (as many places do), because it was relatively peaceful (due to the export of violence to other places). A place where peasants weren't going to be enslaved, sold to Raksha, cursed by wicked gods, etc. But now it's falling apart as the strong Queen is dead and the greedy regional nobles divide things up. But I think people were primed to expect &quot;the Realm is evil and cackles and twirls its moustache!&quot; so that's how they read it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T07:01:02-08:00","id":1350639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant#post1350432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>***HETERODOX VIEWS FOLLOW***YOU HAVE BEEN WARNED***</b><br /> <br /> I'm asking about a PC that you're actually playing rather than one that you theoretically might play or used to play (in an attempt to avoid the NIMBY problem).<br /> <br /> Given that the Realm is a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating murder machine of unreasoning cruelty and injustice without many if any redeeming features, is your current Dynast PC a champion of this evil empire (and thus evil herself) or completely ignorant of it (and thus painfully blind)? Does your PC stand against the Realm? Some other relationship?<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how people play Dynasts as heroic characters. (If your Dynast is herself a corrupt monster, then no need to explain since that's easy to see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Evil&quot; describes just about 99% of all player characters in most games.<br /> <br /> The glourious shining solars founding their own empires and elevating their people to new heights? They're benevolent tyrants, at best. Still tyrants.<br /> <br /> So your question is not exactly very productive. Any and every imperial institution is evil if you so much as assume violating one's right to their own life is evil.<br /> <br /> So you have to judge evil in the context of fantasy, where a war is cool and a slaver is far more of a grim businessman than a villain.<br /> <br /> A good start is to consider that the realm's &quot;incompetence&quot; is very much a mix of recent developments and our own unwillingness to accept a tyrant as anything but worth of derision.<br /> An empire doesn't sustain itself for a thousand years without being <b>good</b> at it. Life in the Blessed Isle is probably the best in Creation, even for the peasantry. Satrapies are strangled, but are also ordered (some states accept the imperial dominance begrudgingly, others profit from it in the short term). The Wyld Hunt is almost an universal good: most of the threats they hunt are legitimate, and it's very, very easy to sell lunars as evil when they are one of the major sources of terror and destruction from outside.<br /> <br /> And yes, people are very much willing to put up with tyrants, especially when the bills are paid. If you want real life examples you can look at places like Saudi Arabia (for the really obvious ones).<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, then, I have to return you the question: How do you measure evil, when most people accept slavery as morally okay and the Realm's oppression comes with benefits?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T07:10:21-08:00","id":1350641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350630#post1350630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, I didn't see that as a sign the Realm was bad, so much that the Realm was good, but now it's falling apart. Before, the government kept the peasants safe from bandits. Now the ruler has vanished, the local nobles are squabbling, the centre cannot hold, and banditry rises.<br /> <br /> I mean, in the rest of the world there's plenty of banditry. It's just normal. The Blessed Isle is somewhere where banditry is unusual.</div> </div> </div> </div>So unusual it's the first thing we see in a book detailing the Blessed Isle! :P<br /> <br /> Eh, I'm less actively objecting to it, I agree it's not so much a sign the Realm is bad. It's more me trying to draw a contrast with the Elana comic, which I view as a highpoint of showing the potential of Dynasts to act more heroically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I agree with you about &quot;who should be in charge, Dragonblood or Solars&quot; being something that there shouldn't definitely be an answer to. (I mean, I'd personally argue both are getting stuck in a certain view of the world, but that applies to both so it's fine).<br /> <br /> But I think a crumbling and malevolent Realm is still something you can argue about, because maybe the Solars are <i>worse</i>. Any northern town threatened by the armies of the Bull of the North is not going to go &quot;oh yes, everything would be better under Yurgen Kaneko and his barbarian horde of fanatics.&quot; I'll be honest, your average Dynastic Dragonblood is probably a better person than the Dawn PC I play alongside.<br /> <br /> If the Realm was nice, and efficient, then you wouldn't be able to answer this question because the Bronze Faction is right and the Gold is wrong. </div> </div> </div>*shrugs* I can make a case for Yurgen or his followers pretty easily. Fighting to throw off oppression, looking to govern ultimately with a loose hand. The setting goes on at length about the evils and exploitative nature of the Realm, especially via the Satrapy system. Yurgen? Err... honestly about the only thing I've got is the Tanlin (sp) and that's an obscure fluff point. Beyond that... he uses Tiger Warriors?<br /> <br /> The argument that the Solars could be worse is rooted in active lore on the First Age of some stripe. Without it, and with the only in setting knowledge coming through the Immaculate Order, Ex3 downplays that ambiguity. While I as an Exalted fan want the setting to remain contentious here, I'm really not sure the devs or writers feel the same way. Morke may have gone but I still feel Ex3 leans fairly hard pro Solar return.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tbh, I kind of think this is Hatewheel's fault. He said that the 2nd ed stuff about the Realm was imperialist apologia, and he wanted to show much more clearly that the Realm is a parasitic empire built on lies and exploitation. A lot of people were like &quot;Woah! Not sure I like this new approach!&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, he liked to portray the Solars as heroes, and talked on forums about this. Yet the game's fluff still has the Bull of the North (even if Lyta and Havesh are no longer mentioned). It still gives them primary allies whose powers are based on cannibalism and who are even more devoted than in 2nd edition to taking peaceful societies and turning them into weapons for a millenia-long war against the Realm.<br /> <br /> And then when the Realm came out (which was not written by Hatewheel or Holden), it showed a country that, well, was actually one of the nicer places to live in Creation, even if it does have exploitative nobles (as many places do), because it was relatively peaceful (due to the export of violence to other places). A place where peasants weren't going to be enslaved, sold to Raksha, cursed by wicked gods, etc. But now it's falling apart as the strong Queen is dead and the greedy regional nobles divide things up. But I think people were primed to expect &quot;the Realm is evil and cackles and twirls its moustache!&quot; so that's how they read it. </div> </div> </div>That was not just hatewheel. The most memorable quotes on that came from Stephanls, to the point IDR Morke saying anything on the Realm specifically. (I'll go diggin in that old quotebank if you're curious. IDR the actual wording but there was at least one saying something very close to 'Dynasts are for people who are okay playing Sabbat in VTM: if that's not you, go play a different Exalt type.) I really feel you're misremembering here Wiz, though to be fair there's a fair chance I am instead. It was a while back. <br /> <br /> I.... unsurprisingly don't agree that I'm just overreacting to things? :P Like, I don't agree with your reading of the Realm portraying the Isle as a straight up nice place to live, but it was not full fronted 'imperialism sucks'. My issue with The Realm is more that it dials the falling apart aspect up. It's grasping, exploitative, falling to pieces... it's really hard to defend not just because it's evil but because it feels like it's practically already fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T08:35:07-08:00","id":1350648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350641#post1350641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So unusual it's the first thing we see in a book detailing the Blessed Isle! :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I guess I could have explained that better. The Blessed Isle <i>was</i> somewhere banditry was unusual.<br /> <br /> I do see your point with the Elana comic though. I think that certainly the Dragonblood book could have done with a bit more of Dragonblood being awesome (that doesn't have to be good. Just awesome).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *shrugs* I can make a case for Yurgen or his followers pretty easily. Fighting to throw off oppression </div> </div> </div>Not really. The Icewalkers weren't a Realm satrapy or anything. They were poor, but not really oppressed. One of the key things Yurgen has done is, well, brought oppressive authoritarian government to them for the first time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The argument that the Solars could be worse is rooted in active lore on the First Age of some stripe. Without it, and with the only in setting knowledge coming through the Immaculate Order, Ex3 downplays that ambiguity. While I as an Exalted fan want the setting to remain contentious here, I'm really not sure the devs or writers feel the same way. Morke may have gone but I still feel Ex3 leans fairly hard pro Solar return. </div> </div> </div>I'd say it leans soft pro-Solar, but I can't deny it does lean one way. Though so did 2nd ed. I think 2nd ed went in a lot for how Solars were going to restore all this ancient magic and technology and make everything wonderful with Wyld-Shaping Prana. Though it also put more effort into showing you the bad Solars than 3rd ed does, I think a lot of which is from Morke's stated approach of showing that the Solars are heroes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'Dynasts are for people who are okay playing Sabbat in VTM: if that's not you, go play a different Exalt type. </div> </div> </div>Best Vampire game we ever played. I got bored of it eventually (shortly after they got back from Hell), but my players begged me to run it again. John Ronin the katana-wielding, trenchcoat-wearing Salubri antitribu who'd break into people's houses and kill them for their Die Hard DVDs, the Lasombra with shadows for bones, the Minotaur Tzimisce, the sharkman Tzimisce the other PCs kept trying to leave behind, and of course their leader Salim... and that was just the Skull Killers, later they teamed up with Machete Justice. Although that alliance would all end in tears and Diablerie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really feel you're misremembering here Wiz, though to be fair there's a fair chance I am instead. It was a while back. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, fair enough, I may well be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My issue with The Realm is more that it dials the falling apart aspect up. It's grasping, exploitative, falling to pieces... it's really hard to defend not just because it's evil but because it feels like it's practically already fallen. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... I guess that the previous edition was more &quot;the Realm is <i>about</i> to fall apart&quot;. A more accelerated collapse gets you to the action quicker, rather than spending 2 years playing its inevitable fall that your ST railroads you to. But on the other hand, if you and the ST want to run the plot of &quot;PCs stop it from falling&quot; that's much harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-24-2019, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T08:41:27-08:00","id":1350649,"title":"","content":"I don't understand how people can draw accurate conclusions about Ex3 and Solars yet.<br /> The logical place to be really cynical about the First Age and question if the Solar Exalted really have any legitimacy beyond might makes right is the Abyssal and Infernal books.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T09:27:47-08:00","id":1350652,"title":"","content":"Of the two dynasts I've played, the first was a cynical reformist working hard as a magistrate to root out corruption with no regard towards personal advancement and not afraid to get his hands dirty to do so.<br /> The second one is a mercenary martial artist who doesn't mind doing house Nellens' dirty work so long as it pays well, and only really cares about fighting strong opponents and accumulating personal glory.<br /> So... pretty much both ends of the spectrum I'd say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T10:01:20-08:00","id":1350659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350648#post1350648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I guess I could have explained that better. The Blessed Isle <i>was</i> somewhere banditry was unusual.<br /> <br /> I do see your point with the Elana comic though. I think that certainly the Dragonblood book could have done with a bit more of Dragonblood being awesome (that doesn't have to be good. Just awesome).</div> </div> </div> </div>The other high note is with Cynis Denovah Avaku My god the 2e comics were awesome. I miss them so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. The Icewalkers weren't a Realm satrapy or anything. They were poor, but not really oppressed. One of the key things Yurgen has done is, well, brought oppressive authoritarian government to them for the first time. </div> </div> </div>*shrug* Fair read, but this is more reading between the lines and interpretation. The only real downside of Yurgen's rule I can remember being given clearly is that he abandoned Icewalker tradition. IIRC his rule was generally noted as good and fair, with his people happy. Other nations were afraid of him, Halta and Linowan after everything that happened at Futile Blood, but that was more about military force and strength - not what kind of ruler he was. People just don't like an outsider taking over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Best Vampire game we ever played. I got bored of it eventually (shortly after they got back from Hell), but my players begged me to run it again. John Ronin the katana-wielding, trenchcoat-wearing Salubri antitribu who'd break into people's houses and kill them for their Die Hard DVDs, the Lasombra with shadows for bones, the Minotaur Tzimisce, the sharkman Tzimisce the other PCs kept trying to leave behind, and of course their leader Salim... and that was just the Skill Killers, later they teamed up with Machete Justice. Although that alliance would all end in tears and Diablerie. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I mean, fair? But I'm muuuuch more a Cammy type. I'll play evil, but I usually swing Lawful Evil - ruthlessness in service to some sort of ideal or a bigger picture. I like characters who can believe they're doing right, and who have to question that via the narrative<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmmm... I guess that the previous edition was more &quot;the Realm is <i>about</i> to fall apart&quot;. A more accelerated collapse gets you to the action quicker, rather than spending 2 years playing its inevitable fall that your ST railroads you to. But on the other hand, if you and the ST want to run the plot of &quot;PCs stop it from falling&quot; that's much harder. </div> </div> </div>Even 'PCs take it seriously' is harder. When you've reached a point where everyone is explicitly out for themselves and willing to screw the Realm as a whole for a slightly larger piece of the pie, it's hard to play a character who believes in the Realm. Who is proud of their country enough to overlook shortcomings and failures. Even if you want to test that faith, to show the Realm's flaws, you need ground for belief first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350649#post1350649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand how people can draw accurate conclusions about Ex3 and Solars yet.<br /> The logical place to be really cynical about the First Age and question if the Solar Exalted really have any legitimacy beyond might makes right is the Abyssal and Infernal books.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* That's true, but it's changes to Ex3 that led to that. Moving the First Age's presentation in the core book more into myth and history tilts the view of the setting to one focused on the present - where there's little firm reason to be cynical about Solars beyond Immaculate doctrine. Contrasted with Ex2 which ultimately kinda leaned Solar but allowed more ambiguity - the epilogue comic with Kejak alone is something I'd hold up, that I don't think Ex3 matches.<br /> <br /> And... that's not a straight up criticism. Ex3 doesn't feel like it's <i>trying </i>to paint Solars as ambiguous. All those new locations, all these Adversaries entries, they could've gone down that well, showed just a handful of returning Solars in a light akin to what the Lunars got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T10:09:14-08:00","id":1350665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350641#post1350641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was not just hatewheel. The most memorable quotes on that came from Stephanls, to the point IDR Morke saying anything on the Realm specifically. (I'll go diggin in that old quotebank if you're curious. IDR the actual wording but there was at least one saying something very close to 'Dynasts are for people who are okay playing Sabbat in VTM: if that's not you, go play a different Exalt type.) I really feel you're misremembering here Wiz, though to be fair there's a fair chance I am instead. It was a while back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I threw it into google and found <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/necro-exalted-3e-where-we-ask-the-writers-about-dragon-blooded.674909/page-25#post-16449912\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T10:26:07-08:00","id":1350671,"title":"","content":"Huh. Not a direct link to the quote I had in mind but it's requoted up thread<br /> <br /> &quot;I think we're just going to say straight out what the Scarlet Dynasty is up to in the Threshold in the corebook and in The Realm, and make Dynastic society as complex and fascinating as it's always been in The Realm and Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought (more fascinating, if possible\u2014culturally some of the Great Houses tended to blur together in 1e and 2e), and people will want to play Dynasts can play Dynasts. It's not like anybody's ever had trouble playing cutthroat Camarilla politics or Sabbat brutality in Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> ...well, no, some people do have trouble playing that. For them we have at least a half-dozen other types of Exalt to play.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T10:27:47-08:00","id":1350672,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d like to share my experience STing a campaign of 3E DBs that lasted a few months.<br /> <br /> What I found out is that it\u2019s extremely *Easy* for dynasts to act tyrannically. Especially when they are caught between conflicting interests of satrapial officers and local government. At one point, the players granted a monopoly on opium(which was prohibited in the satrapy before) to one of the major local noble families, this was an under-the-table deal in an economically precarious situation made to garner political support, without concern for the overall wellbeing of the locals. Normally the players (and to an extent the characters, who were trying to act as &quot;good&quot; people when possible) would have tried to find an alternate solution, but they were very pressed for time and the local noble family jumped at the chance to get the monopoly, so it was the obvious choice. <br /> <br /> <br /> These are the same PCs who fought to push an education reform program that favoured the masses, who earned the respect of the local old guard through honourable action. And who faced down multiple threats to the satrapy. None of this makes them not be representatives of a tyrannic colonial system of exploitation. In the end the reason they were there was the jade, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Later in the campaign they were faced with a conundrum: a pair of lunars had managed to convince a mining town to stop giving tribute and kill their local officials. The PCs first contact ended in disaster as negotiations broke down, the Anathema revealed themselves and the DB and their forces were driven off. When they rallied and returned the found the town on fire and all the residents fleeing away with the Anathema, seeking to cross the borders of the satrapy. The Anathema showed no intention to fight and requested passage under an oath to never return. So what do the PCs choose here? Fight and endanger the nearby civilians(who at this point would defend the Lunars) and potentially fall, having annulled the Lunars' oath? Or let the threat go alongside the population of a whole mining town?<br /> <br /> <br /> In the end they fought, if only because of dogmatic hatred of Anathema.<br /> <br /> The campaign fell through before the fight could really get going. Which was probably a good thing, STing that was bad for my poor revolutionary heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12778-rustedair","name":"RustedAir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T10:41:16-08:00","id":1350675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350659#post1350659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... that's not a straight up criticism. Ex3 doesn't feel like it's <i>trying </i>to paint Solars as ambiguous. All those new locations, all these Adversaries entries, they could've gone down that well, showed just a handful of returning Solars in a light akin to what the Lunars got.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... Second Age Solars appear to still be in their state of quasi-existence where aside from the Bull of the North's circle and a few others they're optional characters that the ST decides if they include or not rather than true NPCs that you can go and find.<br /> <br /> I don't understand this approach but I've come to terms with the fact that I'm not the target audiance for decisions regarding Solars, it's not entirely unlike the relationship I've had with Space Marines in that regard. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T12:31:45-08:00","id":1350689,"title":"","content":"Breaking my own suggestion about going over old stuff, I would say yeah, that Stephen and Holden and not John probably were in the driving seat on talking a lot about framing the Realm as a default antagonist and about extractive imperialism &quot;because it's a real issue in our world&quot;, which marked up some faultlines (in terms of it actually places you in the position of debate with them about if they're actually right about the facts of what they're talking about). <br /> <br /> While John really said far less and more from a &quot;I'm framing it this way because it's one goddamn hell of a story&quot; perspective, where he let his prose speak for itself as a story, without a wider cultural framing or argument trying to persuade you. Which in some ways is less dividing because you're just in a position of agreeing with him about whether it is a story you're interested in or not. Though of course as noted and as was typical for him in discussing all things 3e core related it's &quot;...one goddamn hell of a story... where shining Solar heroes are *the* protagonists!&quot; which also marks up its own faultlines. That's just how it looked on forums though, you could perhaps infer that he may have had different reasons in private and just been more into control of what he said online.<br /> <br /> Essentially I kind of feel like it is right that, unless you've invested the time to read through the 3e Dragonblooded, Realm and Lunars books (which I will admit I haven't really, so am of absolutely limited use in this discussion!), the impression you're gonna be left with is kind of gonna be framed by what Stephen and Holden said they were going to do, and why they said they were going to do it, because the other / subsequent writers mainly liked to let the books themselves tell it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T13:45:56-08:00","id":1350697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350675#post1350675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... Second Age Solars appear to still be in their state of quasi-existence where aside from the Bull of the North's circle and a few others they're optional characters that the ST decides if they include or not rather than true NPCs that you can go and find.<br /> <br /> I don't understand this approach but I've come to terms with the fact that I'm not the target audiance for decisions regarding Solars, it's not entirely unlike the relationship I've had with Space Marines in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it almost makes sense as an outgrowth of Solars are the Heroes. Like, Solars are there to be the driving force, affecting the setting and causing societal change. They're the PCs of another story - so downplay them via the scale of Creation so they don't overshadow the PCs of this one?<br /> <br /> Eh, that's trying to think of a reason behind it. I don't really get it for sure either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T16:07:04-08:00","id":1350721,"title":"","content":"Also, the fact Solars are so new. That's a really key part of the setting, but 2nd ed sometimes seemed to forget how new and inexperienced they are, and how few of them will have managed to find another Solar to team up with, let alone 3-5.<br /> <br /> Not having canon Solars around helps with that idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T17:36:31-08:00","id":1350740,"title":"","content":"Man this prompt is some real &quot;have you stopped beating your wife&quot; level of presumption. <br /> <br /> I'm the ST, and I threw a Wyld Hunt at my players this weekend. At first there was a tense scene along the lines of Inglorious Basterds where they were imposed upon by three Hunt Captains while staying at the house of a PC Solar's Dragonblood Father-in-Law. They barely managed to avoid being caught thanks to the Intimidation Focused Zenith convincing them to leave early. <br /> <br /> Those 3 captains were on their way to purge a Solar Allied Island because, yknow, Heresy. The Solars had to stop them. <br /> <br /> They had a fight, and it was a Major naval battle that turned into a merciless slaughter. The leader of the Wyld Hunt fought valiantly to the end, and when he knew his death was inescapable he took it with dignity and defiance. <br /> <br /> He was dogmatic, driven, and by all accounts evil, but seeing him marshall his men, fight against the Sun Demons, lead the charge directly, and die without yielding made the Solars feel absolutely terrible. Drained. <br /> <br /> The other 2 captains were doing their duty to hunt pirates and instill order. Killed. One Water Terrestrial dove into shark infested water to physically hold his ship's rudder in place so they could escape the hurricane. He was killed by a Lunar ensuring his men had a chance to live. <br /> <br /> It very much felt like parts of Romance of the Three Kingdoms, where noble heroes on opposite sides must occasionally fight, and worthy, moral, heroic men die because they are opposed politically. <br /> <br /> Turning the Realm and the Houses into Good vs Evil is throwing away a lot of nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T18:11:46-08:00","id":1350743,"title":"","content":"So here's the problem isn't that bad. Oh there's corruption, there's bad things that it does but its basically just an empire. The problem with the thesis is it very much makes the position of any Dynast that isn't actively trying to destroy The Realm in the hopes of replacing it with something of modern sensibilities the bad guy regardless of all other things. Essentially the best case scenario by it would be that your character is too much of a fool to come to the conclusion of destroying it all, or you're as much a monster as Raksi is portrayed.<br /> <br /> I mean by this logic attempting to stop the Realm Civil War would be the work of a villain or an idiot. There isn't grounds for someone who's goal is based on the fact that lots of people will die and gods only knows what kind of havoc and destruction will occur from the fighting between houses and a lot of problems from whoever takes over unless they have the doomsday button backing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T18:30:25-08:00","id":1350748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350697#post1350697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it almost makes sense as an outgrowth of Solars are the Heroes. Like, Solars are there to be the driving force, affecting the setting and causing societal change. They're the PCs of another story - so downplay them via the scale of Creation so they don't overshadow the PCs of this one?<br /> <br /> Eh, that's trying to think of a reason behind it. I don't really get it for sure either.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is the Solars who are canonical are some of the worst for potentially overshadowing the PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350721#post1350721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the fact Solars are so new. That's a really key part of the setting, but 2nd ed sometimes seemed to forget how new and inexperienced they are, and how few of them will have managed to find another Solar to team up with, let alone 3-5.<br /> <br /> Not having canon Solars around helps with that idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not convinced it does. The Bull's Circle are the majority of the Solars who clearly do exist outside of comics and fiction, it's lone inexperienced Solars who seem badly underrepresented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 11-24-2019, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T20:47:48-08:00","id":1350761,"title":"","content":"I could do with a few more powerful characters in general who decide they don't really want much to do with the world. They'd still be great story hooks because &quot;powerful person who is not currently being driven to action&quot; just begs to be convinced to be found, but it leave room around them too. Or ones with smaller goals that are nevertheless difficult, or the implication that without intervention maybe won't be possible at all. Like how the new Solar circle is losing in Jiara and maybe needs some help, or how the DB circle is clearly in trouble. That way I'd feel less like I should be considering what the Bull of the North will be doing when I'm putting together my Dreaming Sea game. I mean, I don't really consider it, but sometimes I feel like I should be, which is weird.<br /> <br /> <br /> My new go-to for &quot;I wanna be a dynast but not evil, how?&quot; is HBOs Chernobyl show. I don't think anyone who hates on western imperialism is going to excuse the USSR, and the heroes of that series don't make it their goal to tear down the Soviet Union and crush it into rubble, but they're definitely heroic. Even in real life it's petty hard to get a monument called &quot;Monument to those who saved the world.&quot; without doing something a bit heroic.<br /> <br /> There's an infernal cult that's siphoning the life essence of an entire town to fuel the summoning of a second circle demon, who will then do who knows what. Yes, the Jade in your powerbow was mined by exploited workers, but even if you know that you might not know how to fix that problem. I don't think it makes you evil for ferreting out the cultists, both sparing the innocent from overzealous prosecution, and stopping the guilty, rather than blindly throwing away everything you have in a blunt attempt to fix problems that every superpower has. Certainly not any more than it makes everyone on this forum evil for using a device that requires unsustainably mined copper, dubiously moral Asian labor to assemble, and disposal practices that leave poor areas of poor nations steeped in poison. Even if the device you're using didn't have any of that, somehow, I guarantee some of the tools used along its lifecycle did. The practice might be evil, some of the people involved almost certainly are, but not everyone touched by it automatically is.<br /> <br /> I mean if you want to surge forth and make yourself empress and then find a way to change the Realm so that it's a giant nation without oppression or corruption, and doesn't use its power as leverage against smaller nations unfairly, and all while maintaining enough wealth for upkeep and convincing the upper class that they don't need to be so decedent, that could be fun. That's a pretty big ask though, especially since step one is stopping the civil war, which is going to be hard enough already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T22:13:04-08:00","id":1350767,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m of the opinion that exaltation tends to magnify the personality of the exaltee. Good become great, wicked become worse and all that, but an individual being able to have an outsized impact on the world will always have consequences, personal, societal or global.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m in a game with Croakamancer, and by contrast, my ex-immaculate Zenith is interested in taking down the realm, but mostly because she\u2019s against inequality of all stripes. Her background is that of a rural peasant, one who was given an education and power in a setting where such things are so rare as to be nonexistent. Her values are honest work, and a guarantee of a secure life free from fear of sudden, terrible hardship. To her, the Realm is a construction of terrible inequality and inefficiency which maximizes Unnecessary suffering for the benefit of an elite minority, and that cannot stand. Ditto kingdoms, trade monopolies, spirit courts and the very existence of Soulsteel. She literally would not be able to settle down until she can be sure no injustice is happening within her sight or knowledge.<br /> <br /> While she\u2019s an E2 monk traveling with her circle to save the world, this viewpoint makes her a hero. Once she\u2019s beaten down every Exalt-level threat within reach? Then it gets more complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T23:57:35-08:00","id":1350777,"title":"","content":"I think most Dragon Blooded aren't evil (though some certainly are!). Rather most Dragon Blooded are somewhat callous to the suffering of mortals. Remember that they're basically born and groomed in a society that teaches them from birth that Dragon Blooded are superior to mortals physically, mentally and spiritually. Most of them &quot;drank the koolaid&quot; and believe it (and to be fair it's pretty self-evident that Dragon Blooded <i>are</i> superior to mortals in various very observable ways).<br /> <br /> Dragon Blooded absolutely care about individual mortals they're close, family members, battle buddies, and such but most probably view mortals as a whole more like resources that can be expended or replaced when needed, especially the older ones who live for centuries (and it's primarily those old ones who dictate policy) Of course there are examples in the books of the Immaculate monks protesting and challenging Exalted and high ranking officials for abusing mortals, so there are certainly some Dragon Blooded who understand that they have responsibilities towards mortals as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T04:07:17-08:00","id":1350790,"title":"","content":"What a great thread!<br /> <br /> I always think that these kind of debates need to be (or might benefit from being, YMMV, obvs) rooted in the cultures that they emerge from.<br /> The Bull of the North for instance. Clearly a tyranical warlord leading a campaign of conquest in which tens of thousands are dying. Clearly evil. Except for his people, constant warfare is pretty much the norm. The Northern barbarians weren't some peaceful, idyllic types, they were nomads that constantly fought, traded and fought again with everyone around them. They kind of got the shitty end of the stick from the larger city states in the region. So the Bull's leadership has probably given them wealthy, self-respect, pride and unity. They've stopped killing each other and directed their violence against those that have historically oppressed and abused them. To the Northern barbarians the Bull of the North is a gods damn hero. Sure, his rule is law, but it isn't like the old chiefs were any less strict.<br /> <br /> Dynasts too are the product of an imperial engine built to extract wealth from other nations (the Threshold) and funnel it back to the Blessed Isle. The Empress had made damn sure that she was irreplacable so that no one COULD replace her. With her around, the realm worked. The law was strict but everyone knew where they stood. Peasants had to bow their heads to the Dragonblooded, but the Dragonblooded made sure that the peasants were bothered by plague, bandits, invasions and had a standard of living unimagineable elsewhere. And don't forget that because of the work of the legions, the peasants of the Blessed Isle are well aware of how awful everywhere else is by comparison. Legionnaires returning home after being pensioned out would be telling their families &quot;You won't believe me but some of the places I've been they didn't even have roads. The farmers had to push through dangerous wilderness to get their goods to market. And bandits everywhere. Our temples are much better too, and those places didn't have hospitals. They even had gods doing whatever they wanted, without any monks to keep them in line&quot;.<br /> Life on the Blessed Isle was good. Who wouldn't want to defend that. Clearly the dragonblooded heroes that kept it going were the good guys, protecting their home.<br /> Of course to the Satrapies and the Threshold in general, they were reavers, tyrants and slavers. Brutal overlords who sucked the wealth of the nation right out. Sure, they bought law and order, but only so the jade would keep flowing. And if you tried to resist, they'd burn your neighbourhood to the ground and move in new people with the explicit warning &quot;This could be you, so behave&quot;. Only a monster would support that kind of regime.<br /> <br /> Playing a hero doesn't mean playing someone without flaws, look at any Greek hero. Most of them were terrible in some way or another. But PCs can be heroes or evil in the bounds of their own culture. Picture a dragonblooded swordswoman. Her word is her bond. She is deeply honourable, pious, treats everyone according to their status but with noblesse oblige. Even to the merest farmer she is courteous, although of course she won't accept any disrespect. She fights the anathaema, volunteering for the Wyld Hunt. She is a hero to the culture of the Blessed Isle. However, she also led the legion that put down the rebellion in Ahlat. Her means were strict. She killed one out of every ten people, confiscated land and moved whole populations around. Sure, she stopped he uprising and ended in a year a civil war that might have raged for 20 years, but to the people of Ahlat, she is a butcher, a monster.<br /> <br /> Now picture the converse. A dragonblooded wastrel. His family disapprove of his seemingly infinite affairs, drunken incidents, brawling with commoners. He doesn't take instruction well, shows a lack of respect for his family and his house. He doesn't seem much interested in working with the system to maintain law and order. When he leaves (encouraged by his family) for a tour of the Threshold, he falls in with rebels, starts working against the Realm. Even treats with anathaema. He would be viewed as a base traitor and heretic by the people of the Isle, a perfect example of how low a dragonblood can fall. But to the people of the Threshold he is a hero. A man that could never tolerate the hypocrisy and tyranny of an unjust system and when finally put in a place where he could make a difference acted on his conscience and stood up for the weak and oppressed.<br /> <br /> Heroism is often just based on the culture that views it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T06:44:53-08:00","id":1350812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350790#post1350790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What a great thread!<br /> <br /> I always think that these kind of debates need to be (or might benefit from being, YMMV, obvs) rooted in the cultures that they emerge from.<br /> The Bull of the North for instance. Clearly a tyranical warlord leading a campaign of conquest in which tens of thousands are dying. Clearly evil. Except for his people, constant warfare is pretty much the norm. The Northern barbarians weren't some peaceful, idyllic types, they were nomads that constantly fought, traded and fought again with everyone around them. They kind of got the shitty end of the stick from the larger city states in the region. So the Bull's leadership has probably given them wealthy, self-respect, pride and unity. They've stopped killing each other and directed their violence against those that have historically oppressed and abused them. To the Northern barbarians the Bull of the North is a gods damn hero. Sure, his rule is law, but it isn't like the old chiefs were any less strict.<br /> <br /> Dynasts too are the product of an imperial engine built to extract wealth from other nations (the Threshold) and funnel it back to the Blessed Isle. The Empress had made damn sure that she was irreplacable so that no one COULD replace her. With her around, the realm worked. The law was strict but everyone knew where they stood. Peasants had to bow their heads to the Dragonblooded, but the Dragonblooded made sure that the peasants were bothered by plague, bandits, invasions and had a standard of living unimagineable elsewhere. And don't forget that because of the work of the legions, the peasants of the Blessed Isle are well aware of how awful everywhere else is by comparison. Legionnaires returning home after being pensioned out would be telling their families &amp;quot;You won't believe me but some of the places I've been they didn't even have roads. The farmers had to push through dangerous wilderness to get their goods to market. And bandits everywhere. Our temples are much better too, and those places didn't have hospitals. They even had gods doing whatever they wanted, without any monks to keep them in line&amp;quot;.<br /> Life on the Blessed Isle was good. Who wouldn't want to defend that. Clearly the dragonblooded heroes that kept it going were the good guys, protecting their home.<br /> Of course to the Satrapies and the Threshold in general, they were reavers, tyrants and slavers. Brutal overlords who sucked the wealth of the nation right out. Sure, they bought law and order, but only so the jade would keep flowing. And if you tried to resist, they'd burn your neighbourhood to the ground and move in new people with the explicit warning &amp;quot;This could be you, so behave&amp;quot;. Only a monster would support that kind of regime.<br /> <br /> Playing a hero doesn't mean playing someone without flaws, look at any Greek hero. Most of them were terrible in some way or another. But PCs can be heroes or evil in the bounds of their own culture. Picture a dragonblooded swordswoman. Her word is her bond. She is deeply honourable, pious, treats everyone according to their status but with noblesse oblige. Even to the merest farmer she is courteous, although of course she won't accept any disrespect. She fights the anathaema, volunteering for the Wyld Hunt. She is a hero to the culture of the Blessed Isle. However, she also led the legion that put down the rebellion in Ahlat. Her means were strict. She killed one out of every ten people, confiscated land and moved whole populations around. Sure, she stopped he uprising and ended in a year a civil war that might have raged for 20 years, but to the people of Ahlat, she is a butcher, a monster.<br /> <br /> Now picture the converse. A dragonblooded wastrel. His family disapprove of his seemingly infinite affairs, drunken incidents, brawling with commoners. He doesn't take instruction well, shows a lack of respect for his family and his house. He doesn't seem much interested in working with the system to maintain law and order. When he leaves (encouraged by his family) for a tour of the Threshold, he falls in with rebels, starts working against the Realm. Even treats with anathaema. He would be viewed as a base traitor and heretic by the people of the Isle, a perfect example of how low a dragonblood can fall. But to the people of the Threshold he is a hero. A man that could never tolerate the hypocrisy and tyranny of an unjust system and when finally put in a place where he could make a difference acted on his conscience and stood up for the weak and oppressed.<br /> <br /> Heroism is often just based on the culture that views it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and that's what made past editions of Exalted great.<br /> <br /> I believe, in real life, in objective morality. But Cultural relativism is what makes Exalted great.<br /> <br /> Then 3E hit and brought with it a set of objective moral judgements -- like slavery is wrong. Now, of course slavery is wrong, but if you're going to put that in a book about a society that practices slavery then you're introducing an objective judgement. You're not saying &quot;The Realm are heroes to themselves and villians to their enemies&quot;, you're now saying &quot;The Realm thinks they're heroes but they are objectively wrong.&quot; And that wonks the dynamic somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T07:38:54-08:00","id":1350820,"title":"","content":"&quot;Do you dream there's an alternative? The gods, demons, Fair Folk, dead, and Anathema are all more inhuman and less reliant on mortals than we are. Imagine Creation under the rule of those carrying out alien agendas without pragmatic concern about the well-being of the population, and tremble. Call me a champion of evil if you like, but know that I'm the champion of the <i>lesser</i> evil.<br /> <br /> &quot;And knowing that, be clear. The moment you move from simply advocating reform to opposing the Dynasty, you'll have chosen the greater evil. Then it will be the work of righteousness to cut you down.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T08:29:23-08:00","id":1350827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350812#post1350812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, and that's what made past editions of Exalted great.<br /> <br /> I believe, in real life, in objective morality. But Cultural relativism is what makes Exalted great.<br /> <br /> Then 3E hit and brought with it a set of objective moral judgements -- like slavery is wrong. Now, of course slavery is wrong, but if you're going to put that in a book about a society that practices slavery then you're introducing an objective judgement. You're not saying &quot;The Realm are heroes to themselves and villians to their enemies&quot;, you're now saying &quot;The Realm thinks they're heroes but they are objectively wrong.&quot; And that wonks the dynamic somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I jute re-read the part about slaves in The Realm and I didn't find it &quot;moralizing&quot;. Maybe there are other parts in the book that say that but I don't remember a specific line saying that The Realm is morally wrong because of slaves &quot;in canon&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T08:40:40-08:00","id":1350830,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s worth pointing out too that there have been pretty serious abolition movements in the Realm\u2019s past. None of them fully successful but if you wanted to play Dynast Abraham Lincoln I bet you\u2019d have a hell of a good time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T07:46:55-08:00","id":1351039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350675#post1350675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... Second Age Solars appear to still be in their state of quasi-existence where aside from the Bull of the North's circle and a few others they're optional characters that the ST decides if they include or not rather than true NPCs that you can go and find.<br /> <br /> I don't understand this approach but I've come to terms with the fact that I'm not the target audiance for decisions regarding Solars, it's not entirely unlike the relationship I've had with Space Marines in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>This must just be me but I almost never use &quot;existing NPC's&quot; in any world I'm playing. Solar and first Exalted 3e game was a blessing for me : Descriptions of towns and things nearby, but not tons of NPC's with 1000 years of history about how they formed this specific kingdom and blablabla. I don't think it's bad, to play the intricacies of Dragon Blooded I'm very happy to have The Realm, but the Solar Core gave me all the place I wanted to put a simili-Egyptian Realm that had the narratives tropes of The Princes of Amber and it was the best time for a Solar game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T18:34:41-08:00","id":1351195,"title":"","content":"The main feature of canonical NPCs is that they exist in the setting by default.<br /> &quot;What do you think of the Bull of the North?&quot; &quot;Is it true Raksi eats babies?&quot; &quot;is Mnemon going to be the next Empress?&quot; are the sort of things that (for better or worse) your PCs can discuss without you actively introducing any of those characters. They're actually a liability for encounters because their intimacies and charms could end up being scrutinised by your players prior to their characters actually meeting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T23:50:43-08:00","id":1351234,"title":"","content":"(Slight OT)<br /> <br /> I was having a conversation about accents and the I am David reference just hit me. Kudos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T01:12:44-08:00","id":1351430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1351195#post1351195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main feature of canonical NPCs is that they exist in the setting by default.<br /> &quot;What do you think of the Bull of the North?&quot; &quot;Is it true Raksi eats babies?&quot; &quot;is Mnemon going to be the next Empress?&quot; are the sort of things that (for better or worse) your PCs can discuss without you actively introducing any of those characters. They're actually a liability for encounters because their intimacies and charms could end up being scrutinised by your players prior to their characters actually meeting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a very personal matter. When I discover a world (never played Ex3 before) I don't like being drowned in NPC's, and Exalted 3E Core got this perfect for me. But I'm more than happy to have detailled lunars and dragon blooded afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T07:36:53-08:00","id":1351859,"title":"","content":"I'm not suggesting the corebook should have a number of Solar Exalted NPCs that your PCs are supposed to know about.<br /> <br /> Of those three names I listed in my previous post I think you could easily not know who the Bull or Raksi were without coming across as ignorant. Mnemon's a little trickier because there's a Great House that's projected much further than the personal reputation of its founder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T07:52:17-08:00","id":1351863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1351859#post1351859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not suggesting the corebook should have a number of Solar Exalted NPCs that your PCs are supposed to know about.<br /> <br /> Of those three names I listed in my previous post I think you could easily not know who the Bull or Raksi were without coming across as ignorant. Mnemon's a little trickier because there's a Great House that's projected much further than the personal reputation of its founder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I'll try to be clearer with my answer because I think I didn't explicitly said what I was trying to argue : As someone who totally discovered Exalted with Exalted Core 3e, I was very happy to have few NPC's of importance because it made me not feel like I was disrespecting the world when playing with all the stuff to care about. I think for new players it's an advantage to not have too much NPC's (and solars) written, that was my intended point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T08:26:00-08:00","id":1351870,"title":"","content":"That's fair.<br /> <br /> If it had a Storytelling section I'd want it to address the canonicity of the signature circle. Not everyone whose going to read those Chapter fictions is going to go &quot;oh this Volfer is a cypher character who exists to show me what my Dawn Caste should be like&quot;. They're one of the single largest investments of artwork and word count in the book someone might as well address what happens if one of your players wants to go and meet them because that advice could be applied to other power blocs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T10:07:53-08:00","id":1351881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1351870#post1351870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fair.<br /> <br /> If it had a Storytelling section I'd want it to address the canonicity of the signature circle. Not everyone whose going to read those Chapter fictions is going to go &quot;oh this Volfer is a cypher character who exists to show me what my Dawn Caste should be like&quot;. They're one of the single largest investments of artwork and word count in the book someone might as well address what happens if one of your players wants to go and meet them because that advice could be applied to other power blocs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having Jiara in the setting chapter and referenced in WFHW doesn't help with that impression - establishing the setting for the Solar sigs, having them interract with Mnemon - just on the books, I'm not sure anyone would get the cypher thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T11:31:54-08:00","id":1351887,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...<br /> When I read the 5th ed DnD Player's Handbook, I didn't think the characters in the chapter fiction were people I could expect to interact with, nor the pictures in the Class sections. But you are right about Jiara and Perfect Soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T17:14:39-08:00","id":1352078,"title":"","content":"The setting changes Ex3 has brought to the Realm have led to some soft retcons of why my renegade Dynasts left the Realm. <br /> <br /> Back when I made them in Second Edition the arranged marriages represented a really low (this could be the basis a dystopian YA novel) bar for why it actually sucked to be a Dynast with all those servants and money. Ex3 did a lot to downplay the consequences of not participating in the system of arranged marriages, making the whole thing the setting equivalent of first world problems.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T19:12:08-08:00","id":1354035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1351887#post1351887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm...<br /> When I read the 5th ed DnD Player's Handbook, I didn't think the characters in the chapter fiction were people I could expect to interact with, nor the pictures in the Class sections. But you are right about Jiara and Perfect Soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its quite different in DnD, the core characters are just other adventurers who aren't terribly more meaningful than anyone else, just tougher and richer. They retire when the Exalted begin. <br /> <br /> There are only 300 Solars. I like the idea that there are some non-pc Solars out there having there own stories and changing things. I designed a whole adventure in the South as basically &quot;You guys left the West and jumped into the middle of soneone else's campaign&quot;. It makes the world seem more real, to me. <br /> <br /> You aren't the only force in Creation, its a living world that other incredible god-kings are changing around you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T20:42:05-08:00","id":1355112,"title":"","content":"In a 2.5 game I played a house Cathak Sorcerer (she deliberately chose that to ostracize herself from the social life of DBs and get more space to herself) who was an agent of the Reclamation- she had Stanewald as a mentor, and was convinced that uniting the forces of the old Titans with those of the Realm was the only true way to create a prosperous future for creation. The stability of a unified Realm combined with the raw cosmic power of the old Titans would allow them to eliminate suffering, expand creations boarders, and create peace without strife. She also had a lover/employer from Lookshy, as she studied abroad there during her sorcery training (House Cathak was more than happy to put her out of sight and out of mind) and fell for someone; on top of that she had ties to the locust crusade, although we didn't get to flesh that out in play much. She was Compassion 1, conviction 4, manipulation 4. Good person? Probably not how a passerby or her house would describe her- consorting with Demons, in bed with Lookshy, condescending and egotistical, but at the same time her beliefs and motivations came from genuine goodwill and a philosophy of compassion. Didn't express that in person really, figures it's usually a waste of time to be nice to people, she's got a bigger mission after all! Not that any of these dullards could truly comprehend it, all caught up in their stupid social graces and immaculate dogma. <br /> So, ignorant, I suppose, maybe &quot;evil&quot; as well? She wasn't the run of the mill evil/ignorant dynast though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25854-santova","name":"Santova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T12:35:50-08:00","id":1355679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1352078#post1352078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting changes Ex3 has brought to the Realm have led to some soft retcons of why my renegade Dynasts left the Realm.<br /> <br /> Back when I made them in Second Edition the arranged marriages represented a really low (this could be the basis a dystopian YA novel) bar for why it actually sucked to be a Dynast with all those servants and money. Ex3 did a lot to downplay the consequences of not participating in the system of arranged marriages, making the whole thing the setting equivalent of first world problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amata Kinslayer's backstory with her husband serves as a counterpoint to WFHW as a much more traditional portrayal of arranged marriage right down to a controlling and abusive husband.<br /> Which I appreciate because it's such a common trope in fiction that it shouldn't feel closed off to people playing a Dynast for the first time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T13:40:17-08:00","id":1355690,"title":"","content":"While I agree with the comments that disagree with the OPs characterization of the situation and the Realm:<br /> <br /> Mnemnan Amal: Earth Aspect who favored Medicine who went with the entourage of a new satrap to the West. Besides designing and building several new immaculate temples and monasteries, he also used (rather too much) of the budget on improving clean water infrastructure, improving farming methods, and establishing hospitals. During some of his downtime, he used his medicine charms on the poor and orphaned (rich people had to make an appropriate donation to the temple). The newly built monasteries had an overabundance of young monks who idolized him and there was a bit of a worry that he was being personally worshiped as a byproduct of &quot;local superstitions&quot;.<br /> <br /> His motivation wasn't exactly pure benevolence. He believed that freedom from a lot of the worst problems in life made people free to contemplate the dragons and render spiritually beneficial service to the Realm and the Exalted. Starving children don't chant sutras and a population suffering from disease isn't producing tribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T14:55:30-08:00","id":1357607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1355679#post1355679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amata Kinslayer's backstory with her husband serves as a counterpoint to WFHW as a much more traditional portrayal of arranged marriage right down to a controlling and abusive husband.<br /> Which I appreciate because it's such a common trope in fiction that it shouldn't feel closed off to people playing a Dynast for the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I would not begrudge anyone using that element in their backstory. Its just drawing from some very patriarchal ideas, particularly when we are talking about the typical starting character who recently graduated secondary school.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T22:07:54-08:00","id":1357679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1350675#post1350675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not the target audiance for decisions regarding Solars, it's not entirely unlike the relationship I've had with Space Marines in that regard. </div> </div> </div> </div>I hate how much this contextualized my antipathy towards a lot of the decisions around Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T22:34:17-08:00","id":1357685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1357679#post1357679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate how much this contextualized my antipathy towards a lot of the decisions around Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T01:11:24-08:00","id":1357719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1357685#post1357685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are Space Marines. (Pressumably the 40k kind.)<br /> <br /> Vanilla super-humans who are the best of the best (except not really) ruled over by an untouchably distant golden god (who mostly just leaves them to their own devices), in a setting where they confront powerful demons, aliens and existential horrors as (more-or-less) equals.<br /> <br /> Solars and Space Marines have rich and varied fluff and flavour, but both face the stigma of being &quot;bland&quot;. Juice them up with the powers if hell! Play a less powerful, more interesting faction! Be a robot! Be a normal human, hopelessly outclassed! Human but better? Blah.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's possible that I misread Lioness and Steamfunk but that was my reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T03:17:58-08:00","id":1357731,"title":"","content":"The main issue I have with Solars that most reminds me of Space Marines is how it's consistently been considered <i>unthinkable</i> to have access to a version of the core rules without the Solar Exalted, especially this edition where the stuff exclusive to playing a Solar accounts for like a third of the corebook.<br /> <br /> I've personally carved up the setting and game material into pieces relevant to my Dragon-Blooded players but I shouldn't have to of done that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T05:51:38-08:00","id":1357752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1357731#post1357731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main issue I have with Solars that most reminds me of Space Marines is how it's consistently been considered <i>unthinkable</i> to have access to a version of the core rules without the Solar Exalted, especially this edition where the stuff exclusive to playing a Solar accounts for like a third of the corebook.<br /> <br /> I've personally carved up the setting and game material into pieces relevant to my Dragon-Blooded players but I shouldn't have to of done that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I can also quibble all day about how various design decisions make the game very challenging to GM if players make really standard assumptions. But the real problem I have is that I would prefer a version of exalted where Solars are part of the setting. The devs for 3e are on record stating that, to them, solars *are* the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T08:33:37-08:00","id":1362119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant#post1350432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the Realm is a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating murder machine of unreasoning cruelty and injustice without many if any redeeming features, is your current Dynast PC a champion of this evil empire (and thus evil herself) or completely ignorant of it (and thus painfully blind)? Does your PC stand against the Realm? Some other relationship?<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how people play Dynasts as heroic characters. (If your Dynast is herself a corrupt monster, then no need to explain since that's easy to see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div>My DB's someone that is painfully aware of how flawed the Realm is, and how flawed other dynasts are. He's also aware that the Realm is the one thing that prevents Creation from sliding into Anarchy and barbarism (or worse). Realm is not perfect, dynasts may be selfish and exploitative, but at least this system tries to keep as many people safe as possible. From the invasions of the barbarians, predations of the Fae, machinations of the Lunar Anathema that are out to destroy the civilization and drown the world in savagery. From the devastations of wars waged by minor warlords on periphery. From the destruction and corruption brought by demons. From the exploitation done by gods and spirits.<br /> <br /> And while Realm is definitely not perfect, it is there. And an attempt to replace it with something better would be tied to a chaos, devastation and slaughter on unprecedented scale, with the end result unlikely to be any better (but very likely to be far. far worse).<br /> <br /> So, he might try to fix the problems he sees, the things he is capable of fixing, but standing against the realm would be unthinkable. One would have to be irresponsible, misguided, insane or a monster to do that.<br /> <br /> And anyone claiming that &quot;the Realm is a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating murder machine of unreasoning cruelty and injustice without many if any redeeming features&quot; is either lying, or completely ignorant (and thus painfully blind).<br /> <br /> By the way, out of all my Exalted characters, that one is probably the most moral, selflless, heroic and righteous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 01-20-2020, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T08:49:33-08:00","id":1362122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's also <b>aware </b>that the Realm is the one thing that prevents Creation from sliding into Anarchy and barbarism (or worse).</div> </div> </div> </div>Indoctrinated, you mean. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">at least this system tries to keep as many people safe as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't the people be safer if they didn't have to give increasingly large portions of their food and resources to an imperial overlord who'll bury them up to their necks and leave them to animals if they miss a payment?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the invasions of the barbarians...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which they might've had a chance at fighting off or negotiating with themselves, if they had the resources...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...predations of the Fae...</div> </div> </div> </div>...as above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...machinations of the Lunar Anathema that are out to destroy the civilization and drown the world in savagery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Destroy <i>the</i> civilization. As in, <i>the Realm</i>. By taking on Chiaroscuro and Wavecrest as satrapies, they're painting silver targets on them. <br /> <br /> \u200b(Also, not every Lunar is 2e Ma-Ha-Suchi this time around.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the devastations of wars waged by minor warlords on periphery.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the devastations of wars waged by up-jumped princes out to &quot;sow their oats.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the destruction and corruption brought by demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the destruction and corruption brought by bureaucrats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the exploitation done by gods and spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the exploitation done by greedy and lusty overlords.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while Realm is definitely not perfect, it is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read the chapter fiction with Strawmaiden Janest? Where was the Realm?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And an attempt to replace it with something better would be tied to a chaos, devastation and slaughter on unprecedented scale, with the end result unlikely to be any better (but very likely to be far. far worse).</div> </div> </div> </div><i>People governing themselves? Oh, noes! D:</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362119#post1362119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, he might try to fix the problems he sees, the things he is capable of fixing, but standing against the realm would be unthinkable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, people subjected to indoctrination are often conditioned to consider opposing it unthinkable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T09:04:54-08:00","id":1362127,"title":"","content":"What I like in Exalted is, when I play a Dragon-blooded I can fully play thinking like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar434_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"434\" data-vbnamecard=\"434\">Astralporing</a> character, and the I play a Solar/Lunar I can fully play like commented by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> , and I don't feel dissonant at all, it just seems natural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T10:20:23-08:00","id":1362148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which they might've had a chance at fighting off or negotiating with themselves, if they had the resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might not necessarily be as easy as it seems at first. If the Realm crumbled away it would leave a lot of room open for other empires to spring up all over with the same problems. Some small nations currently under Realm control wouldn\u2019t be in close enough proximity to care much right away, others would fall to their more powerful neighbors, and others would become the new conquers. Cherak is ripe to form its new conquering empire, for example. Of course the people on the Blessed Isle would also suffer greatly.<br /> <br /> The Realm is like any historically large and powerful nation, it\u2019s a symptom of human pride and avarice. If you want to solve the actual problem problem and not just knock down Creations superpower de jour you\u2019re really going to have to fix a deeper problem. Any form of government will lead to some people having a lot of power, and they will all have to refrain from using that power to gather more power and security. <br /> <br /> If you actually want to have fun playing Lunar Skywalker battling the Empire though, you should probably just not think about that. I\u2019d also look to flossing over a lot of the factional fighting and crimes that are common to rebel groups the world over. Otherwise it\u2019s not so much a game as your ST sitting there lecturing you on how you\u2019re bad people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T10:21:46-08:00","id":1362150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>People governing themselves? Oh, noes! D:</i></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mortals will not be left to govern themselves; it is obvious that the gods, elementals, demons, Fair Folk, dead, Anathema, and other Dragon-Blooded will all scramble to take power if the Realm falls. If you oppose the Realm, all you are doing is choosing to change the master. And if you dare not name the new master you're serving, hiding behind the slogan of 'people governing themselves', the only reasonable conclusion is that you know you would be torn to pieces in the streets if you spoke the truth.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T10:33:30-08:00","id":1362153,"title":"","content":"Rankar VII of Gem is a mortal; while the Perfect of Paragon and some members of the Council of Entities are some stripe of sorcerer, they're all still human. Wavecrest's Feathered One and the inhabitants of the Coral Palace in the Neck might well be some stripe of God-Blooded (<i>probably</i> - I don't remember for sure at this point), but don't necessarily command much in the way of supernatural powers. The degree to which mortal communities are dominated by the supernatural tends to get drastically overplayed by some here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-20-2020, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T10:46:41-08:00","id":1362159,"title":"","content":"Exalted isn\u2019t great for that though. The problem is primarily that there are charms for governance and leadership in Bureaucracy and War and stuff. A Dragonblooded commander definitely 100% benefits from nepotism, but she\u2019s also the general because when a mortal commander sounds the charge her troops charge in courageously, when a DB commander sounds the charge the sky rains fire down upon the enemy and her troops become completely immune to fear. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s really bad for a democracy too because a Solar performance Supernal would just crush his mortal debate opponents with the weight of Solar arete. Exalted\u2019s just not a good setting for that kind of story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T10:58:12-08:00","id":1362166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362159#post1362159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted isn\u2019t great for that though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet the characters I've mentioned are written into the setting; I hadn't even gotten into the Guild yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362159#post1362159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is primarily that there are charms for governance and leadership in Bureaucracy and War and stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but consider for a moment that the Exalted aren't everywhere, nor are they necessarily obsessed with micromanaging every tribe of herdsmen making dough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362159#post1362159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Dragonblooded commander definitely 100% benefits from nepotism, but she\u2019s also the general because when a mortal commander sounds the charge her troops charge in courageously, when a DB commander sounds the charge the sky rains fire down upon the enemy and her troops become completely immune to fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is he even fighting them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362159#post1362159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s really bad for a democracy too because a Solar performance Supernal would just crush his mortal debate opponents with the weight of Solar arete. Exalted\u2019s just not a good setting for that kind of story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did I say &quot;democracy?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bNegotiating from weakness is still a thing, you guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-20-2020, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T11:20:37-08:00","id":1362171,"title":"","content":"Mortals with political power is definitely a thing that can and should happen, but in Exalted the world will end up with Exalts running most of the highest positions. It might appear to be a glass ceiling based on discrimination but actually it\u2019s because the exalted really just are more capable people.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not like Avatar Legend of Korra where benders were in charge because fire hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T11:25:42-08:00","id":1362173,"title":"","content":"Even so, competence and capability are not the end-all, be-all of who gets to wear a crown.<br /> <br /> \u200bShit, that's more evident now than ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T11:38:29-08:00","id":1362178,"title":"","content":"It's probably worth noting that not all Exalts want or are good at being in charge, and as there's a small number of Exalts, they're probably not enough to fill most leadership positions. There's also the way DBs tend to be congregated, while Solars+Lunars may indulge in nepotism that will make it difficult for other Solars+Lunars later (no, you can't be king, you're not descended from the great snake-emperor!).<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, Solars can be the best administrators in the world... But in the entire world there's 6 supernal bureaucrats. 6! 6. 6! That's not hyperbole. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying to not expect Exalted to be over-represented in power. But power isn't always meritocratic, and there aren't that many.<br /> <br /> I mean, I guess this depends what we mean by &quot;highest position.&quot; That's superlative, so we're talking about like, what, 5 jobs in the world? So maybe that will be true, but it's hardly shocking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-20-2020, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T12:30:54-08:00","id":1362194,"title":"","content":"Even in cases where it\u2019s not meritocratic though the Exalted have an advantage. You might have somebody up for election who\u2019s dumb as a brick, but when she gave her opening speech announcing her intent to run for office the steams and rivers of the nation swelled, for even the very mountains wept with joy. Or even just somebody who gets people to follow him because he purports to be a strong man who will protect them and that\u2019s reenforced by the fact that he can pick up a boulder the size of a house and chuck it to the horizon. Not every exalt is going to be the best example of that kind of exalt, but if we\u2019re saying that they\u2019re truly mythic heroes then that\u2019s going to put them in a drastically advantaged position. That\u2019s not even counting the lifetimes or even millennia of experience they could accrue. <br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded are especially prone to ending up like that because they fuse nepotism with magical abilities. It\u2019s just going to be hard to get a lot of places where the mortals aren\u2019t being ruled or influenced in some way by the Exalted, which isn\u2019t really fair.<br /> <br /> I like the snake emperor descendant though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T12:41:16-08:00","id":1362199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362194#post1362194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s just going to be hard to get a lot of places where the mortals aren\u2019t being ruled or influenced in some way by the Exalted, which isn\u2019t really fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard is fine. Unfair is fine. I'm just not convinced it's inevitable or invariable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362194#post1362194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the snake emperor descendant though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T13:18:32-08:00","id":1362206,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s kind of getting away from my main point anyway which is that if you just leave people alone to govern themselves a lot of the time they\u2019re going to form some kind of empire on their own. So you have to leave them alone, except when one of them gets the idea that since their kingdom is 3 times as large and powerful as their neighbour maybe their neighbour should give them some extra favourable trade deals. Or maybe they get attacked by their neighbour and win the ensuing war and then decide that\u2019s not going to happen again so they\u2019re just going to go ahead and keep it. <br /> <br /> You\u2019re going to have to stop your nation from doing that, and also every other nation that\u2019s in a position to do so, which is a lot even if you were the only exalt in the world. It\u2019s just a hard problem to solve. You also have an issue if there\u2019s another nearby group that\u2019s doing things you find morally abhorrent for other reasons and maybe want to put a stop to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T13:50:45-08:00","id":1362213,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... Historically, generally when an Empire collapses it isn't quickly replaced by new ones. I am not saying that never happened, of course it did, many, many times, but a bit more often colonies/satrapies/tributaries stay unstable but free, while the main part of the Empire spends a century or two as a set of smaller states. Many of the initial states will soon form into larger ones, but those will generally fail to reach the critical mass that pushes them into an Empire.<br /> For example, after the collapse of the Roman Empire, no state ever managed similar control of the Mediterranean. The province of Britannia was replaced by numerous small kingdoms. By about 400 years later they were replaced with... About 10 (1 bigger than the rest). By 900 years later there was one. By 1200 years later it had absorbed a couple of small kingdoms next to it. But... that's it. Tiny compared to Rome. Yes, Britain did then start its own Empire, but we're talking 1300-1500 years later.<br /> (And 60-75 years after we lost our empire, the vast majority of our former possessions are still independent.)<br /> <br /> Similarly, India was united in the early 1st millennium, IIRC, not to be done again until the 19th century, the middle Eastern Caliphate fell in the 1000s and wasn't resplaced by something of its former power for 600-ish years, Mali and Songhay have never really been replaced, nor, say, Austria-Hungary, or the Khmer Empire. China is the area of the world where Empires have been most likely to be replaced, but there's often been periods lasting centuries where it's not united. I mean hey, Mongolia and Taiwan have stayed out of Chinese rule for 75 years now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T14:25:10-08:00","id":1362231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362178#post1362178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, yes, Solars can be the best administrators in the world... But in the entire world there's 6 supernal bureaucrats. 6! 6. 6! That's not hyperbole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's required to have supernal Bureaucracy to be considered a great ruler Wizard of Oz. While it may help a lot, I think what most really need to become good rulers is the compentency to run an organization, a honorable spirit that does not see others as merely tools to be used, and the wisdom and foresight to understand the consequences of his or her own actions and the actions of his or her own nation, both past actions and future actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T15:29:18-08:00","id":1362253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indoctrinated, you mean. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Biased, perhaps - but not more biased than your point of view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the people be safer if they didn't have to give increasingly large portions of their food and resources to an imperial overlord who'll bury them up to their necks and leave them to animals if they miss a payment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not really. Without submitting to <i>someone</i>, those peasants would usually not be able to defend from most of the dangers Creation is filled with. So, in the end, they'd be giving food and resources to someone either way. Whether that someone would be more or less greedy than Realm, and more or less capable of actually defending them would be highly dependant on the specific situation (and subject to change).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which they might've had a chance at fighting off or negotiating with themselves, if they had the resources...</div> </div> </div> </div>Some threats could possibly be negotiated with, or defended against. Other would require either bigger diplomatic negotiation power or military strength to deal with than many of satrapies have (and definitely more than most of the <i>villages</i> have)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Destroy <i>the</i> civilization. As in, <i>the Realm</i>. By taking on Chiaroscuro and Wavecrest as satrapies, they're painting silver targets on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking as if Lunars were only attacking Realm directly, and not prone to using initially neutral sides as their tools of war. Besides, their modus operandi seems to be exactly the destruction of the industrial level overall, not just in the Realm itself, because they decided that it's something they need far less than Dragonblooded do in order to wage war.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, not every Lunar is 2e Ma-Ha-Suchi this time around.)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not everyone. But some are. And many do not need to be 2e Ma-Ha_Suchi to be considered monsters by the (often innocent) people that get sacrificed in the name of their war with the realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the devastations of wars waged by up-jumped princes out to &quot;sow their oats.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the internal factional war does have casualties, but it is generally limited<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the destruction and corruption brought by bureaucrats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow i don't think that demons of Malfeas and bureucrats (no matter how corrupt) lie in the same category of dangers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the exploitation done by greedy and lusty overlords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exploitation of greedy and lusty overlords would be exactly what would happen if there was no Realm around, so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you read the chapter fiction with Strawmaiden Janest? Where was the Realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>True, in this case it was too far away to help. If it was closer, perhaps the sacrifice of the harvest god, and the destruction of other villages nearby might not have happened. Still the Realm does protect a large part of Creation, and a majority of its inhabitants. Do you see anything that could take its place? Janest might protect a single village, maybe (and even that is not sure - remember, that the chapter fiction does not tell us how that story ended).<br /> Not to mention that the village exists and Janest could be born only because many years ago armies of dragonblooded died in order to protect the creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362122#post1362122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>People governing themselves? Oh, noes! D:</i></div> </div> </div> </div>What, do you really think that after destruction of the Realm, what would take its place would be a shining and peaceful democracy, instead of an anarchy, or a large number of small, warring states? Or that the transition to any new entity taking its place would be peaceful? There would have been wars - long and bloody wars, and while you may think that what would come after would be better, the people living in that era are more realistic.<br /> <br /> Yes, all those views are biased, but are completely reasonable - especially from the point of view of someone living in the Realm. And the point is, you can't really say that they are <i>wrong.</i><br /> <br /> And, personally, i am cynical enough to think, that even if the Realm is the evil, tyrannical empire feeding on the lifeblood of its satrapies, that does not mean that anything that might replace it would be better. Because it probably wouldn't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 01-20-2020, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T15:30:16-08:00","id":1362255,"title":"","content":"You don\u2019t have to be that big to be an empire do you? Maybe not rising right up from a previous empires sphere of influence but there\u2019s been dozens of empires in the last thousand years. Imperial Japan, Inca, Aztec, Ottoman, Holy Roman Empire, Britain, Mongolia, Russian, Sikh, Spanish, French, Zulu, Austrian, American debatably. There\u2019s lots more, those are just some of the biggest. It\u2019s a lot of peoples who decided on their own to go out conquering that you\u2019d have to stop, without yourself conquering anyone including them. <br /> <br /> You\u2019ve got issues pulling back the empire as well, which is pretty evident in the Middle East. There\u2019s some good resources from journalists embedded in with the American troops and local fighters for that kind of thing. There\u2019s a bunch of horrible stuff that you\u2019d expect like American troops finding a local thief and deciding to destroy his car to teach him a lesson, totally on their own with no consequences or thought. Then you\u2019ve got other people working really hard to set up some kind of local security force so that the American soldiers can leave and the Taliban won\u2019t just walk in and take back over, except the locals that they\u2019re working with are a lot more interested in stealing government funds and kidnapping small children for use as sex slaves. Add onto that pressure from back home and from local allies to keep the oil industry happy and continued terrorist attacks in the West and it just gets all muddled and messy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T15:48:32-08:00","id":1362256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronos12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362231#post1362231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's required to have supernal Bureaucracy to be considered a great ruler Wizard of Oz. While it may help a lot, I think what most really need to become good rulers is the compentency to run an organization, a honorable spirit that does not see others as merely tools to be used, and the wisdom and foresight to understand the consequences of his or her own actions and the actions of his or her own nation, both past actions and future actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh indeed! And an honourable spirit is something Exalts posses more of on average than anyone else (Dynasts probably have less, but that's from being dynasts, not Dragonblood).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T16:11:32-08:00","id":1362262,"title":"","content":"Huh... No, you're right.\ud83e\udd14 I mean look at Britain's colonies without us. I've met Botswanans and Kenyans and Zambians and none of them offered to carry me on a palanquin to go elephant hunting! They seemed to think they had as many rights as me, a white man! Can you believe it? You know they even have the gall to elect politicians instead of listening to the wisdom of Her Majesty!\ud83d\ude28<br /> <br /> And don't get me started on the worst of our former colonies... the so-called United States of America.\ud83d\ude20 A blatant rip-off of the United Kingdom, can't even think of their own names! New York? Does it even have viking ruins?\ud83d\ude1d<br /> It's a hellhole of murder, drugs, guns, corruption, and so unfree they don't even have free healthcare! <br /> Now if only they had just known their place and accepted the rules of the Mother of Parliaments. Imagine! Banning slavery decades earlier, gun control, free healthcare, and proper English rather than whatever pidgin illiterate tosser came up with &quot;sidewalk&quot; and &quot;eggplant&quot;. Peace with the American-Indian nations. Instead of having a massive civil war in the 19th century, they could have helped us subjugate, I mean, uh, &quot;civilise&quot;, the less advanced races. \ud83d\ude09 And we'd have shown Hitler what for several years earlier!<br /> <br /> No-one would need to vote Trump to make their country great if they were part of Great Britain! (Plus, what kind of country has so little self-confidence they need to vote for their leader? Just have Her Majesty Elizabeth II, Defender of the Faith, crowned by the Archbishop of Canterbury on behalf of God himself. She can trace her lineage to Adam and Odin, by George!)<br /> <br /> Yes, the fall of an Empire only leads to chaos, destruction, poverty and the conquest by other nations. A quick look at Canada, Malta, Canada, Ireland, Botswana, New Zealand, Barbados, India, Singapore, Trinidad, etc, will show you just what a disaster the fall of the British Empire was! (F*cking ungrateful Irish. After we did such an excellent job dealing with their Popery-caused population growth in the 1840s as well! Why, if the Corn Laws and our administration hadn't worked so well, their population might be three times as high today!\ud83d\ude22)<br /> <br /> (This is a joke. Just to be clear. I hope it doesn't come off as mean-spirited or condescending.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-20-2020, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T22:23:20-08:00","id":1362344,"title":"","content":"Spoilered, for others' sake.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, not really. Without submitting to <i>someone</i>, those peasants would usually not be able to defend from most of the dangers Creation is filled with.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Most of the dangers Creation is filled with&quot; are wolves and tigers. Poisonous mushrooms that look similar to the tasty ones. Rusty tools. Staircases with an unattended toy on them, or ladders with a bad step halfway up. The occasional bad storm that collapses your roof or ruins your harvest. Greedy merchants, exploitative usurers, and men who would sell you bridges. Illness. Weevils, locusts and mosquitos.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Realm protects from none of these, and in fact fosters quite a few of them to use <i>against</i> the peasants.<br /> <br /> Sure, hobgoblins and storm serpents <i>exist</i>, but most people in Creation will go their entire lives without seeing either. And the Realm doesn't proactively go out and take care of these threats; it waits until the raksha has already lured away the farmer's children, and then the farmer's lucky if he's not drafted to help put down the fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the end, they'd be giving food and resources to someone either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd still rather give something than have it taken away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're talking as if Lunars were only attacking Realm directly...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're putting words in my mouth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, not everyone. But some are.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no one has been demonstrated to be 2e Ma-Ha Suchi this time around, not even Ma-Ha Suchi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And many do not need to be 2e Ma-Ha_Suchi to be considered monsters by the (often innocent) people that get sacrificed in the name of their war with the realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But monstrousness is not a desire to tear down civilization itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somehow i don't think that demons of Malfeas and bureucrats (no matter how corrupt) lie in the same category of dangers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right - bureaucrats are far worse than Neomahs are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, in this case it was too far away to help.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Because they distanced themselves when they saw trouble coming</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was closer, perhaps the sacrifice of the harvest god, and the destruction of other villages nearby might not have happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If ifs and buts were candy and nuts, we'd all have a merry Christmas.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still the Realm does protect a large part of Creation, and a majority of its inhabitants.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that a farmer &quot;protects&quot; the pigs as he leads them to the slaughterhouse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you see anything that could take its place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that the village exists and Janest could be born only because many years ago armies of dragonblooded died in order to protect the creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't know that. Can you demonstrate that Janest would never have been born if an emissary of the Shogunate hadn't gone out and negotiated with the Fair Folk, instead of pettily squabbling over resources while the raksha hordes massed at the gates?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, do you really think that after destruction of the Realm, what would take its place would be a shining and peaceful democracy, instead of an anarchy, or a large number of small, warring states?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you people keep cramming the word &quot;democracy&quot; in my mouth?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or that the transition to any new entity taking its place would be peaceful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you people keep cramming the word &quot;peace&quot; in my mouth?<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, it <i>won't</i> always be peaceful. But it'll be smaller, and smaller communities <i>tend</i> to try and make peace more readily, because they don't have as many people to lose before it stops being a viable community.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, all those views are biased, but are completely reasonable - especially from the point of view of someone living in the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, cultures that commit atrocities tend to feed a viewpoint to the people raised inside, with the purpose of guiding them into not questioning atrocities committed to maintain it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362253#post1362253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the point is, you can't really say that they are <i>wrong.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think slavery is wrong?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As for me, I'm not playing a Dynast currently, but one of my players was for a time. He was a House Cynis Wood Aspect who'd gone to Great Forks to see to House interests there; he brought with him two slaves that he grew up alongside, and once he was safely away from the prying eyes of his family, he freed and married them. He's become aware of some of the problems with the system back home, but he's not convinced he knows a solid way forward to fix them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-21-2020, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T00:49:01-08:00","id":1362362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362262#post1362262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(This is a joke. Just to be clear. I hope it doesn't come off as mean-spirited or condescending.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it feels both. <br /> <br /> Also as a Canadian I can tell you the nation of Canada is doing quite well and the First Nations that inhabited this continent before European settlement are still being shit on. Massive disappearances of native women, a mixture of uninvestigated murders and sex trafficking, poor social support, complete lack of trust both ways with law enforcement, incredibly high suicide and drug use rates and little movement towards fixing any of it even with a lot of pressure mounting over the last decade. It\u2019s not good, they went through a terrible genocide of their people and their culture, especially through residential schools that were designed to make them forget everything they learned about their nation from their family, and as it is now they aren\u2019t ever getting their lands back. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really see a simple solution to that. Do you? Maybe we\u2019ll all just head back to where our ancestors came from. I\u2019m sure the hundreds of thousands of Iranian people here are itching to get back to the country that just killed over 100 Canadian and Iranian civilians by accident. Hopefully by accident. The UK and France surely wouldn\u2019t mind several million newcomers either, plenty of space for refugees. We\u2019d all be happy to do it too, so no moral ambiguity in relocating us! Plus the impoverished First Nations should just jackrabbit right up, pulling themselves out of the mire by their bootstraps! The M\u00e9tis people might be a bit of a problem though, I have to say. They\u2019re so deeply intertwined between indigenous and European family lines they\u2019d have a hard time deciding where to go. God damnit, it was all so easy a second ago...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which isn\u2019t even what I was saying in the first place. In modern 2020 Earth massive superpowers keep eachother in check primarily with economic sanctions and trade tariffs and with the ultimate looming threat of MAD if two superpowers ever got down the path to escalation in open war. Creation doesn\u2019t have any of that. You could knock over the Realm, Prasad, Iscomey, Coral, and all the rest and you still wouldn\u2019t really have solved the problem. Good luck doing that in a way that lets you sleep at night too. You\u2019re locking up all the criminals and not addressing the problem of unemployment, poor housing, and nonexistent mental health support. Unless your personal beef is with the Realm and not Imperialism in general in which case go for it, burn it to the ground and your problem is solved.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re going to need a path to get there too, otherwise you\u2019re just being one of those beautiful fools that thinks the way to stop climate change is to stop using all fossil fuels tomorrow*, or thinks that the ills of capitalism should be cured by overthrowing the whole thing and enforcing communism right now. It\u2019s not as easy as that, and you probably want to get there without killing a lot of people, which makes it even harder.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe though, since were playing a game here, you can just simplify it a little so that you can have some kind of happy ending. Or just be Getalt of Rivia and try to stay out of the whole mess because fighting monsters is hard, but at least it\u2019s usually pretty clear who the monsters are. Or just say that it sucks and try not to be one of the worst rebels/imperials. Or ignore the whole thing completely and just blow up the Imperial Manse, get a medal, everyone lived happily ever after. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *please don\u2019t insinuate that because I don\u2019t believe it is a viable option to bring all transport to a grinding halt that somehow makes me an anti-science denier of man made climate change. I am painfully aware of the physics behind the equilibrium of the sun\u2019s light and the Earth\u2019s black body radiation, as well as the feedback loops of increased water vapour, decreased snow cover, and trapped gasses that make that balance more sensitive to CO2 levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T01:36:52-08:00","id":1362364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362213#post1362213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... Historically, generally when an Empire collapses it isn't quickly replaced by new ones. I am not saying that never happened, of course it did, many, many times, but a bit more often colonies/satrapies/tributaries stay unstable but free, while the main part of the Empire spends a century or two as a set of smaller states. Many of the initial states will soon form into larger ones, but those will generally fail to reach the critical mass that pushes them into an Empire.<br /> <br /> For example, after the collapse of the Roman Empire, no state ever managed similar control of the Mediterranean. The province of Britannia was replaced by numerous small kingdoms. By about 400 years later they were replaced with... About 10 (1 bigger than the rest). By 900 years later there was one. By 1200 years later it had absorbed a couple of small kingdoms next to it. But... that's it. Tiny compared to Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but, and I think this converges on Astralporing's point, what came after Rome (in the West) wasn't really much closer to &quot;idealized communities of peoples and nation states govern themselves&quot;. It was rampaging sets of &quot;barbarian peoples&quot; (Avars, Huns, Visigoths, Anglo-Saxons, Franks, Slavs, vikings, Irish Scotii, and so on) establishing themselves as dominant ethnic groups over much smaller territories but over people who were different to themselves, or their own &quot;empires&quot;, and this transitioning over time into an internationalized European aristocracy which heavily intermarried but was often quite alien from the peoples over which it ruled, in its identity. If our goal is &quot;Peoples rule themselves&quot; (or people avoid being oppressed and dominated by people with ethnic identities other than there own) then its not really so clear to me that the fall of the Roman Empire in the short term was really a good thing or got you any closer to that state, if not further away!<br /> <br /> (And this is Rome in the West, because Rome never really fell in the East).<br /> <br /> (Before the rise of the nation state it seems like you have a choice really between A) localized states which approach closer the ideal of a people ruling itself, but aren't really based explicitly on this principle and whose leaders don't act like it, or B) larger states which aren't, but which have wider markets and things like this which can improve living standards by wider trade and policing and specialization.)<br /> <br /> (The end of the British Empire is somewhat of a different thing than Rome, and hard to compare. You have huge changes between Rome to Britain where Britain really is more committed to these ideas of parliamentary self rule which drive contradictions in maintaining an empire, and where it really does diverge economically from world markets that make tax revenues there become increasingly unattractive relative to cost of military footprint, and where the US really takes away as a hegemonic state which is even more committed to democracy (or its appearance!) and which can crucially project intensively from a network of bases with a tiny footprint, doing away any territorial need for huge empire, even to keep the trade routes open to the non-Western places which even matter. The &quot;pointillist empire&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T01:50:38-08:00","id":1362367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362213#post1362213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, after the collapse of the Roman Empire, no state ever managed similar control of the Mediterranean. The province of Britannia was replaced by numerous small kingdoms. By about 400 years later they were replaced with... About 10 (1 bigger than the rest). By 900 years later there was one. By 1200 years later it had absorbed a couple of small kingdoms next to it. But... that's it. Tiny compared to Rome. Yes, Britain did then start its own Empire, but we're talking 1300-1500 years later.<br /> (And 60-75 years after we lost our empire, the vast majority of our former possessions are still independent.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is tangential to the discussion, but you're looking at a wrong place.<br /> <br /> The centre of Roman civilisation around V-VIth century was already farther to the east. We sometimes use to think of Constantinopol as some kind of fan-made version of Rome, but definitely they thought of themselves as completely regular Romans. So, when that remote nowhere of Britannia ceased to be a part of the Empire, it was not a major tragedy. <br /> <br /> And in the east, well, much of the civilisation of Rome was taken over by the newly emergent exploding Arabic empire. Afterwards the Roman empire started generally crumbling with occasional periods of revival, at some point, probably after IVth crusade it completely ceased to be a meaningful power, and the Arabic states fell pray to the newly emergent Turkish empire (and to the emerging power of Venetian empire in the West). <br /> <br /> Generally, we see power vacuum in the Roman West around 5th century, because honestly, no one cared. For the ancient mindset it was clear that the civilisation is from Rome, North Africa, Greece, through Egypt, Babylonia, Persia, Media, to India. Ok, in late antiquity Galia was a civilised place, but then, there was really no power vacuum there and when we read Gregorius of Tours, in VIth century, we see that this is still pretty much an ancient society and both in Italia and in Galia barbaric rulers generally wanted their reign to look legal, e.g. asking Roman Senate to make them consuls. But still, it was definitely not the centre of focus for the Roman Empire. <br /> <br /> We tend to think of northern Europe as place of interest because of much later events. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T05:58:53-08:00","id":1362382,"title":"","content":"I know, but as the Eastern Empire didn't collapse, but rather was conquered by a rival Empire, I didn't feel it was relevant to a discussion on the collapse of Empires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T06:47:21-08:00","id":1362387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362382#post1362382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, but as the Eastern Empire didn't collapse, but rather was conquered by a rival Empire, I didn't feel it was relevant to a discussion on the collapse of Empires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry if my post looked patronising.<br /> <br /> My point is: it's a misconception to think that there were two empires. There were multiple emperors of course, but people of the era clearly thought of them as rulers of the same entity.<br /> <br /> You know, what formally happened in 476 was that rulership over Italia was oficially assumed by the Eastern emperor., so this tells a lot about their perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T07:08:50-08:00","id":1362391,"title":"","content":"Oh certainly, and the East was richer and generally more peaceful anyway. There's a reason Constantine chose the East to settle in and not the West.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T07:14:22-08:00","id":1362393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362364#post1362364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but, and I think this converges on Astralporing's point, what came after Rome (in the West) wasn't really much closer to &quot;idealized communities of peoples and nation states govern themselves&quot;. It was rampaging sets of &quot;barbarian peoples&quot; (Avars, Huns, Visigoths, Anglo-Saxons, Franks, Slavs, vikings, Irish Scotii, and so on) establishing themselves as dominant ethnic groups over much smaller territories but over people who were different to themselves, or their own &quot;empires&quot;, and this transitioning over time into an internationalized European aristocracy which heavily intermarried but was often quite alien from the peoples over which it ruled, in its identity. If our goal is &quot;Peoples rule themselves&quot; (or people avoid being oppressed and dominated by people with ethnic identities other than there own) then its not really so clear to me that the fall of the Roman Empire in the short term was really a good thing or got you any closer to that state, if not further away!</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I believe* most archeological research now indicates that, in Britain at least, the Britons mostly integrated peacefully with the Angles, Saxons and Jutes, and actually British people in 450-600 lived on average 2 years longer than during the Roman period.<br /> <br /> But honestly, I was talking about... hmmm, I guess the medium term rather than the short term.<br /> <br /> <br /> *From what I've read. Professor Robin Fleming's book Britain after Rome, for example. I won't claim to be a professional in this area, my MA is in Modern History, not early medieval, it's just a period I find interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T07:28:05-08:00","id":1362398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362362#post1362362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it feels both.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry. My group, being English and Welsh, makes a lot of parody jokes to each other about imperialists in our games. Especially Dragonblood games. People playing explicitly racist imperialists who talk about how &quot;Thresholders make great troops when led by Realm officers!&quot; and &quot;the Realm Citizen's burden&quot;. It maybe doesn't come across well to others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also as a Canadian I can tell you the nation of Canada is doing quite well and the First Nations that inhabited this continent before European settlement are still being shit on. </div> </div> </div>I know, but I don't think that's because Canada is no longer being ruled by Britain. Our parliament tended to make nice-sounding pronouncements while the governors on the ground continued their racist policies, terror squads, divide and rule, etc, and generally got away with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t really see a simple solution to that. Do you? </div> </div> </div>No, but I wasn't really trying to give one. Just saying that the collapse of the British Empire did not lead to Canada inevitably being invaded or becoming its own empire.<br /> <br /> Alhough honestly Canada's not really a good example anyway, when talking about the Realm; places like Botswana, Nigeria, Jamaica and India are better. Canada's a place the British used primarily for settlement (post the loss of the USA), which the Realm doesn't do, they just take control of other nations in order to extract resources and enforce their ideology and geo-political aims.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe we\u2019ll all just head back to where our ancestors came from. </div> </div> </div>No way or we letting Trump claim British citizenship from his British mum, no way!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *please don\u2019t insinuate that because I don\u2019t believe it is a viable option to bring all transport to a grinding halt that somehow makes me an anti-science denier of man made climate change. I am painfully aware of the physics behind the equilibrium of the sun\u2019s light and the Earth\u2019s black body radiation, as well as the feedback loops of increased water vapour, decreased snow cover, and trapped gasses that make that balance more sensitive to CO2 levels. </div> </div> </div>I wasn't intending to, I do understand. I like you DrLoveMonkey, you're good for this forum, I'm not trying to be mean.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps, instead of trying to make clever points, I should just boil down my argument to a simple point:<br /> I do not believe, based on history, that when an Empire collapses the formerly-ruled nations will inevitably become empires or get conquered by other empires. Sometimes yes, of course! But not always. Thus, saying &quot;if the Realm falls it might be replaced by something as bad&quot; isn't a great argument for the existence of the Realm, because things might stay the same, or they might get better.<br /> <br /> (There's a point about how the fall of Empires tend to involve civil wars, and those are generally horrible. But the Realm's about to fall into a Civil War anyway, so...)<br /> <br /> Now, saying all of this, I could definitely imagine a Dynast <i>believing</i> that if the Realm falls it will inevitably be replaced by another Empire, and using that to justify it to themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T08:30:12-08:00","id":1362414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362398#post1362398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, instead of trying to make clever points, I should just boil down my argument to a simple point:<br /> I do not believe, based on history, that when an Empire collapses the formerly-ruled nations will inevitably become empires or get conquered by other empires. Sometimes yes, of course! But not always. Thus, saying &quot;if the Realm falls it might be replaced by something as bad&quot; isn't a great argument for the existence of the Realm, because things might stay the same, or they might get better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important in Exalted to place your reflexion at the level of your character. You are playing a Demi-god of the mightiest power on Creation, that enforces order one way or another, and you are purposed to extend this order all your long life.<br /> <br /> When someone argues, inside Exalted, says that &quot;If the Realm falls it might be replaced by something as bad&quot; or &quot;If the Realm falls it might be replaced by something terrible&quot;, they don't make a general statement about historical study of Empires, they make a political statement on their core belief of what will happen next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T12:09:36-08:00","id":1362478,"title":"","content":"Many things are empires which are neither called that nor possess many of the trappings, such as an emperor. They also varied greatly in size. The Delian League, or rather the Athenian Empire, was significantly smaller and less populated than even many small modern nation-states.<br /> <br /> One definition of empires is: ...a state where one set of people (the core) extract resources (typically by force) from another set of people (the periphery) [From <a href=\"https://acoup.blog/2019/11/22/collections-why-are-there-no-empires-in-age-of-empires/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>]<br /> <br /> As that source argues, there has never really been a time when there were not empires and nation-states, which Creation has a relative overabundance of, are something of a historical aberration. Empires, of whatever size, may well be the most common and most dominant form of social organization for all of history.<br /> <br /> Replacing the Realm will almost certainly give rise to numerous small empires as regionally strong states attempt to make the best of the situation. This is, funny enough, what most PCs get up to if a game runs long enough because the nascent Realm Civil War provides a prime chance to begin carving out power bases and spheres of influence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am having trouble quoting CountAlucard's message, but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd still rather give something than have it taken away.</div> </div> </div> </div>That they are framed as voluntary gifts to the king does not mean they aren't really taxes. The difference is that more of them will go toward local uses, which might be more investment in local infrastructure or might be the king having bigger parties that he used to be able to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T12:53:43-08:00","id":1362490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362393#post1362393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I believe* most archeological research now indicates that, in Britain at least, the Britons mostly integrated peacefully with the Angles, Saxons and Jutes, and actually British people in 450-600 lived on average 2 years longer than during the Roman period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but probably by the standards people mostly &quot;integrated peacefully&quot; with the Roman Empire and Roman identity? <br /> <br /> 2 years longer seems like a pretty fine life expectancy estimate difference for what you can know through archaeology, but I don't know very much about how these things are worked out and I haven't read anything of that length, and could have many different causes.<br /> <br /> (I also think it's very hard to work out what degree to which integration is peaceful, or integration even happened rather than a change from the archaeology from the little I know. Forensic archaeology, isotopes, material culture, studies of skeletal trauma, are all very difficult and noisy indicators that can end up saying very little that is not malleable to interpretation.).<br /> <br /> Would say it's a good point for sure worth reminding us that the Western Roman Empire didn't immediately get replaced by the Langobardic Empire or the Hunnic Empire or something (and so on for similar examples) - that is a reductive tendency that can end up presenting without really thinking it through. But I would say that this is a bit of a unintentional reduction on the part of anyone who seems to be pointing it forth; the real point is more that the dynamics that led to the rise of empire don't tend to fall with one big empire, and the reason why another does not arise after are more due to constraints in the actual capabilities of &quot;challengers&quot; who try to put one back together again and much less due to, well, falls in people *wanting* to build one up or trying to (as if the rise of these big empires were due to ideas which are a freak occurrence, not a more general condition).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T13:12:45-08:00","id":1362495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362478#post1362478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One definition of empires is: ...a state where one set of people (the core) extract resources (typically by force) from another set of people (the periphery) [From <a href=\"https://acoup.blog/2019/11/22/collections-why-are-there-no-empires-in-age-of-empires/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>]</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like a bit of a questionable definition though; China's empires generally extracted from their demographic core of the river deltas (through tax) in order to fund military expenditures and &quot;civilization&quot; at the frontier. All the better to keep the barbarians at bay. Still an empire. Tons of what we call empires did that - even Rome, which is a fair example of an empire that really did tax elsewhere and spend in Italy wasn't extracting resources in Britannia, for ex, as much as expending resources gathered in their core in both armies and civilization possibly existed pretty much by central imperial fiat and expenditure of resources gathered elsewhere. Empires can't really be defined by where they gather resources and where they expend them.<br /> <br /> (Some of this comes from arguments that empires must exist because of some economically extractive &quot;profit&quot; motive which come from certain kind of materialist economic schools of thought. But, and I'm sounding like a stuck record here, but this is to ignore ideology, military considerations, prestige, and the fact that even when there is an economic motive, it may only benefit some people with political sway, and not the actual people who are paying the expenditures.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T15:48:26-08:00","id":1362746,"title":"","content":"Leaving the spoiler tags on, in order not to spam too much.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1362344#post1362344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Most of the dangers Creation is filled with&quot; are wolves and tigers. Poisonous mushrooms that look similar to the tasty ones. Rusty tools. Staircases with an unattended toy on them, or ladders with a bad step halfway up. The occasional bad storm that collapses your roof or ruins your harvest. Greedy merchants, exploitative usurers, and men who would sell you bridges. Illness. Weevils, locusts and mosquitos.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Realm protects from none of these, and in fact fosters quite a few of them to use <i>against</i> the peasants.<br /> <br /> Sure, hobgoblins and storm serpents <i>exist</i>, but most people in Creation will go their entire lives without seeing either. And the Realm doesn't proactively go out and take care of these threats; it waits until the raksha has already lured away the farmer's children, and then the farmer's lucky if he's not drafted to help put down the fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Numerically, most of the dangers are indeed minor ones, on a level that can be ignored. There's enough of the bigger dangers however to make an idea of self-protection on the level of individual villages laughable.<br /> <br /> Notice by the way, that the majority of the major dangers would be <i>other humans</i>. From the regions under Realm influence we've heard about, most (if not all) were in a state of war or internal strife before Realm even arrived. And the supernatural dangers do exist, and regions in danger of those don;t seem to be as uncommon as you say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd still rather give something than have it taken away. </div> </div> </div>You do realize, that in most cases the difference would be moot, as individual people on the ground would often not even get asked about what they want anyway. It's not like most of the satrapies Realm conquered were communities created by voluntary assent from bottom to top. Most of the political entities in Creation (well, out of those that are bigger than a single village anyway) are autocratic in nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're putting words in my mouth. </div> </div> </div>No, i'm not. The goal of lunars may be destruction of the realm, but their chosen method <i>is</i> a destruction of industrial infrastructure everywhere. Because a barbaric Creation is a field of battle that suits Dragonblooded the least, while Lunars are not hindered by it in the slightest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure. But monstrousness is not a desire to tear down civilization itself. </div> </div> </div>That very desire is Lunar's battle plan, if you haven't noticed. I'm not saying they necessarily like it (because i am sure most do in fact not like it), but they will still tear down the civilization in order to defeat Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're right - bureaucrats are far worse than Neomahs are. </div> </div> </div>If only Neomahs were the only demons you'd need to be wary of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes. </div> </div> </div>Where? Which other entity is strong enough to protect Creation in the case that, for example, another Balorian crusade, or something on similar level comes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't know that. Can you demonstrate that Janest would never have been born if an emissary of the Shogunate hadn't gone out and negotiated with the Fair Folk, instead of pettily squabbling over resources while the raksha hordes massed at the gates? </div> </div> </div>No, but i can demomonstrate that noone would have been alive in that village (or anywhere else) if most of the shogunate dragonblooded did not die in order to slow down the armies of the Balorian Crusade, and if the Empress didn't use Sword of Creation to stop the Fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do you people keep cramming the word &quot;democracy&quot; in my mouth? </div> </div> </div>I didn't.I pointed out to you that the entities that would replace the realm would almost certainly not be nice countries we're so used to in the 21st century, but most probably just a bunch of smaller, but equally autocratic and exploitative states.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do you people keep cramming the word &quot;peace&quot; in my mouth?<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, it <i>won't</i> always be peaceful. But it'll be smaller, and smaller communities <i>tend</i> to try and make peace more readily, because they don't have as many people to lose before it stops being a viable community. </div> </div> </div>The Realm is built in such a way, that a transition period is guaranteed to be very, very violent. Those smaller communities you speak of, that are more ready to make peace? That might come much after -- but first you'd have years after years of bloody wars and smaller conflicts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right, cultures that commit atrocities tend to feed a viewpoint to the people raised inside, with the purpose of guiding them into not questioning atrocities committed to maintain it. </div> </div> </div>You might consider, even for a second, looking at the situation from the perspective of people living in that place and era, without filtering it through the eyes of someone living in 21st century Earth.<br /> Notice, that in many cases the people Realm commits &quot;atrocities&quot; on would have problem with that not because they think those were atrocities, but simply because they were the victims of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think slavery is wrong? </div> </div> </div>Personally? Yes.Although the better question would be &quot;Do you think that the people of Creation think slavery is wrong&quot;. And the answer to that is not so obvious as you might think.<br /> Hint: even most <i>slaves</i> at the time of Rome didn't think slavery was wrong. They just didn't want to be slaves <i>themselves</i>.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ghosthead added to some of the things i wanted to say, so i will end with only one more response:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for me, I'm not playing a Dynast currently, but one of my players was for a time. He was a House Cynis Wood Aspect who'd gone to Great Forks to see to House interests there; he brought with him two slaves that he grew up alongside, and once he was safely away from the prying eyes of his family, he freed and married them. He's become aware of some of the problems with the system back home, but he's not convinced he knows a solid way forward to fix them. </div> </div> </div>Precisely - even those well aware of the problems with the realm will be unlikely to see any solid way to fix them. Solutions to complex problems are generally neither simple not easy. An ability of individuals to make any lasting, bigger changes would be minimal (and on top of it, being too heavy handed with &quot;fixing&quot; stuff runs the risk of derailing the whole system and generating way more problems than you just tried to solve). And it's very easy to think, that the only way to be able to do <i>anything</i> would require you to work from within the system. Because looking from within, you are extremely unlikely to be able to see any viable alternative (no, 21th century earth systems are not viable, because not only most people would not be even able to imagine them, but they are not something you could easily and quickly introduce).<br /> <br /> It is easy for us to look at the Realm in moral outrage, saying that it needs to be replaced, but actually doing that is a completly different matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T18:03:51-08:00","id":1362771,"title":"","content":"I mostly want to leave this entire conversion alone, but want to add one thing of significance to the current discourse:<br /> <br /> The Marukani are a culture consisting of almost entirely independent homesteads who circumstantially organise into mutual cooperatives under a leadership of limited power.<br /> <br /> They are on friendly terms with a rigidly organised and highly militarised neighbouring state because they don't take liberties and they're able to provide highly skilled cavalry.<br /> <br /> Relationships like this have existed in reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T04:42:39-08:00","id":1363054,"title":"","content":"In the spirit of construction, the Marukan seem a bit like cowboy-Scythians (of the Iron Age, in the western steppe). <br /> <br /> Cowboy in some of the aesthetic and cultural nods (boiled and grilled beef for breakfast on the range!), Scythian in the way that they're not quite totally nomadic pastoralists but have some commitment to settled agricultural sites scattered on a sparse landscape (increasing the archaeology seems to be indicating this, against a narrative of high levels of nomadism, which certainly hold more true for other societys). While still being characterized by relatively high mobility and long range connections dependence on the horse. The relationships with powers more tied into urbanism and sedentary agriculture also seem to have some similarities? <br /> <br /> So this is really just a nod that this set of peoples may be worth looking at if anyone is interested in thinking about how to use Marukan in any stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T06:14:52-08:00","id":1363063,"title":"","content":"Regarding something worse taking the Realm's place.<br /> <br /> I think it's too soon to say for Ex3. Lunars lost a lot of their pretty serious red flags when they were updated and while it seems there's a clear move away from Deathlords as Sauron type villains who the Solars, Lunars, Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded must put their old hatreds aside unite against - necromancy is a force multiplier for how much you can abuse a civilian population and still get the resources you want, more importantly I can't see the writers trying to justify what The Mask of Winters has done to Thorns.<br /> <br /> The other faction of interest here is the Fair Folk because they're emotional vampires who'd run a city like a tyrant as an end onto itself. But the previous editions have been almost monofocused on fae who enjoy negative emotions and after the late 2e errata difficult to say if they're even capable of stepping into that void.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T12:59:57-08:00","id":1363170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363063#post1363063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see the writers trying to justify what The Mask of Winters has done to Thorns.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have been playing far too much Dominions, but I don't feel that The Mask of Winters <i>needs</i> any justification. <br /> He took over a city (everyone does this) by military force (the usual method) and then consolidated his supply lines and borders (in a very unusual way). The value of having an &quot;intact&quot; city is pretty questionable if it's an island of isolated territory. All it really says to me is that when given the choice of being wrong in a military sense and being wrong in a humanitarian sense, we know which decision The Mask of Winters makes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T13:26:35-08:00","id":1363176,"title":"","content":"I don't think he does, but they gave nuance to Raksi while keeping her as a person who literally eats babies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T13:36:01-08:00","id":1363179,"title":"","content":"Some shenanigans led to a duplicate post. I like the slight and deliberate rewording of the other one better.<br /> <br /> To fill space, I'll add that I wouldn't personally expect the Mask of Winters to be depicted as gracious in his governance of Thorns or to have some motive with which we might be expected to sympathise. Maybe not quite so atrocious as to give Abyssal players an impression that he's not viable as a mentor, but still a figure who raises questions for the players to grapple with if they're not quite as down on playing it in terms of ancient world realpolitik.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-24-2020, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T13:37:44-08:00","id":1363180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363176#post1363176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think he does, but they gave nuance to Raksi while keeping her as a person who literally eats babies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly; it states that they're served on platters before rival shahan-yas or their adherents, and that she serves them alive. It seems a bit implicit that the expectation is that such people won't actually do it.<br /> <br /> A chapter fiction depicts her as being coy about somebody relaying the story of her cannibalising enemy soldiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T14:10:03-08:00","id":1363187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363180#post1363180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly; it states that they're served on platters before rival shahan-yas or their adherents, and that she serves them alive. It seems a bit implicit that the expectation is that such people won't actually do it.<br /> <br /> A chapter fiction depicts her as being coy about somebody relaying the story of her cannibalising enemy soldiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It amuses me to think that she probably declines some petitions on account of the petitioner lacking the fortitude to eat the baby, while accepting other petitions on account of the petitioner having the fortitude to defy her by not eating the baby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T16:06:34-08:00","id":1363215,"title":"","content":"<br /> Added bonus, different petitioners at the same meal get those results adding to her perception as a complete madwoman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T05:09:07-08:00","id":1363276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363187#post1363187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It amuses me to think that she probably declines some petitions on account of the petitioner lacking the fortitude to eat the baby, while accepting other petitions on account of the petitioner having the fortitude to defy her by not eating the baby.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, now I'm confused.<br /> <br /> Does Raksi not eat babies anymore? Like, at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T05:43:47-08:00","id":1363282,"title":"","content":"Only in front of guests she wants to flex on, who get served one too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T06:18:32-08:00","id":1363286,"title":"","content":"Does she really do it though ? Or does she resort to some tricks ?<br /> <br /> I think that's something that can be easily interpreted depending on the ST. Not everyone want to play eating-babies important NPCs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T06:56:18-08:00","id":1363291,"title":"","content":"You could do that of course, but I kind of feel it's important to her place in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T15:13:54-08:00","id":1363355,"title":"","content":"And it's not hard to have it both ways considering she doesn't do it to everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T11:00:35-08:00","id":1363820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363291#post1363291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do that of course, but I kind of feel it's important to her place in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T11:19:22-08:00","id":1363828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363820#post1363820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's a visceral exposition of what it means (potentially) to be an Elder Lunar, which lends nuance to the dynamic between the Realm and the Silver Pact. Monsterousness is a central theme to Lunars, much as Werewolf was a game &quot;of savage horror&quot;.<br /> <br /> It dimishes Lunars specifically and Exalted as a whole if Raksi doesn't eat babies. She doesn't have to exclusively, or mindlessly, or needlessly eat babies. But she has to eat live human infants.<br /> <br /> It's like in Fallout 4 where the Institute has you hunt a Synth that's turned into a Raider. Synths being perfectly moral beings who could never murder someone else makes that entire dynamic one sided and just flat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-28-2020, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T11:31:55-08:00","id":1363829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363828#post1363828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it's a visceral exposition of what it means (potentially) to be an Elder Lunar, which lends nuance to the dynamic between the Realm and the Silver Pact. </div> </div> </div> </div>She vivisects captive Dynasts. <br /> <br /> I think that'll be the one that straddles the line between &quot;this is to unsettle visitors I don't like&quot; and &quot;this is something is enjoy doing anyway&quot;. If nobody ever visited her again, any stray Dragon Blooded given to her as a birthday present by her friends and adherents probably aren't facing better prospects.<br /> <br /> Consuming human flesh recreationally made more sense for how they characterized Raksi in First Edition, but it doesn't really fit the overall picture now. That's still a picture of a monster, and not even one who is lacking in disturbing luxuries or gratuitous cruelty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T14:25:46-08:00","id":1363855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363829#post1363829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She vivisects captive Dynasts. </div> </div> </div> </div>Which is utterly meaningless because those Dynasts &quot;started it&quot; by Usurping the Solars and hunting down every Lunar who Exalts as Anathema.<br /> <br /> Doing bad things to a horrific enemy is not remotely the same thing as doing bad things to innocent people.<br /> <br /> Raksi as a baby eating monster can be used to justify the Bronze Faction. Raksi being mean to the people who hurt her and want her dead is very anemic.<br /> <br /> Even if Raksi only eats babies as a political gambit to freak people out, she still needs to be a baby eating monster.<br /> <br /> I'm ok with the text in Fangs just saying that she serves babies to guests of honour and leaving it at that.<br /> <br /> I'm not ok with her explicitly not eating babies at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T15:51:24-08:00","id":1363863,"title":"","content":"This feels like a topic that is more appropriate in the thread about how the Bronze Faction/Realm views Lunars. Do you mind if I quote your post for a response there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T18:54:45-08:00","id":1363889,"title":"","content":"Either way this has become a very strange conversation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T05:03:49-08:00","id":1363947,"title":"","content":"I think this is more about Dragonblood and mortal immaculate-believers than Sidereals.<br /> The bronze faction leaders have a pretty &quot;ends-justify-the-means view. If they thought the world was better off led by Raksi and co, I think Kejak and Syn might accept the baby-eating as the price of doing business.<br /> <br /> Whereas for the non-Sidereal, many believe the Dynasty is necessary because they protect the world from literal baby-eating monsters and their savage hordes. Do you want a Lunar to eat your baby, fuck your horse, replace your husband, and smash your city to rubble? Well, only the Dynasty can protect you (they argue).<br /> <br /> (Do you want a Dragonblood to enslave you and murder your gods? Well, only the Lunars can protect you.)<br /> <br /> Raksi is the Lyta/Havesh of Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> I guess the elders may use the same argument to recruit young, less jaded, Sidereals to the Bronze faction though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T06:02:35-08:00","id":1363951,"title":"","content":"I intend to continue the rest of this conversation in a thread where it belongs, but I will respond to one fairly straightforward line:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363947#post1363947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksi is the Lyta/Havesh of Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third Edition Raksi is much closer to those characters now, because neither of them did anything equivalent to consuming humans of any age, or victimising people that had not wronged or were politically offensive to them at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T06:30:01-08:00","id":1363954,"title":"","content":"Yeah, she's much better written.<br /> <br /> Lysa and Havesh are terrible people, the sort that Immaculates can reasonably point to, the sort that make the Bronze Faction go &quot;crap, the Solars are still dangerous&quot;, but they're written well enough that you don't read their descriptions and they come off as &quot;lol, I lovez evilz and killing for the lulz&quot;. Like many evil people in the real world, there are reasons and ideologies behind their evil, they didn't just wake up pure evil one day and put on a black cloak and start cackling. That doesn't justify their behaviour (except to Solar apologists or Lyta's fanatical followers, of course), but it does explain it.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Raksi is a terrible person, but she's still a three-dimensional character with motivations that make sense. Eating babies is awful, but she's not doing it just because.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T20:04:42-08:00","id":1364676,"title":"","content":"I have an immaculate monk who is, while devoted to the faith, a genuinely good person. She would fall under the ignorant category.<br /> <br /> It's like the concept of any organization where individual members can be a force for good, but the organization itself actually is not. Little Mountain genuinely cares about people. She strives to make sure everyone is their best self they can be while adhering to the doctrine. She does it via compassion and a willingness to step below her station as a prince of the earth.<br /> <br /> In many ways from a publicity standpoint she's an excellent face for the order. &quot;The order cares about you see, this young girl is willing to help you on your path and guide you, surely your next life will be better if you follow what she says!&quot;<br /> <br /> She also is fully a believer. She was raised in the cloister. She's very ignorant to the thought that another worldview might be right. Given she's an isle DB its very likely she hasn't seen the threshold atrocities so has been sheltered to believe &quot;the realm prospers, its people cared for, this must be what they do for everyone!&quot; so yeah, ignorant.<br /> <br /> She would have a real crisis of faith if she saw some of the stuff that went on off the isle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T01:03:52-08:00","id":1364714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363863#post1363863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels like a topic that is more appropriate in the thread about how the Bronze Faction/Realm views Lunars. Do you mind if I quote your post for a response there?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's addressed to me then let this stand as consent to all people for all time: feel free to quote me where ever, when ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T01:09:02-08:00","id":1364715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1364714#post1364714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's addressed to me then let this stand as consent to all people for all time: feel free to quote me where ever, when ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just quoted you for the sake of it, then !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T04:48:31-08:00","id":1365225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant#post1350432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>***HETERODOX VIEWS FOLLOW***YOU HAVE BEEN WARNED***</b><br /> <br /> I'm asking about a PC that you're actually playing rather than one that you theoretically might play or used to play (in an attempt to avoid the NIMBY problem).<br /> <br /> Given that the Realm is a corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating murder machine of unreasoning cruelty and injustice without many if any redeeming features, is your current Dynast PC a champion of this evil empire (and thus evil herself) or completely ignorant of it (and thus painfully blind)? Does your PC stand against the Realm? Some other relationship?<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how people play Dynasts as heroic characters. (If your Dynast is herself a corrupt monster, then no need to explain since that's easy to see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Catching up with a 9-page monster thread is something I find pretty impossible, but I'll assume that multiple people already remarked that the simplistic view and assertions you've made in this post are simply inaccurate.<br /> <br /> First, Exalted is not a game of black-and-white morality. Evil Empires only exist in D&amp;D, where Good and Evil are literal, real and objective forces in the game setting. Exalted is a bit more like A Song of Ice and Fire - one nation's hero is another nation's villain. <br /> <br /> The Scarlet Empire, that you dub a &quot;corrupt, incompetent, baby-eating murder machine of unreasonable cruelty and injustice without many if any redeeming features&quot; is the sole reason that humanity is even a thing anymore in Creation (oh, and that <i>Creation</i> is even a thing anymore in Creation). <br /> Whatever you may think of her, the Scarlet Empress literally saved the world from annihilation. The Realm, far from incompetent, is a bastion of humanity and the strongest, most numerous and most successful military force in the world. <br /> The Realm has many features that you can certainly find cruel, unjust and offensive to real world Western thinking (particularly one of democratic sensibilities). Almost nothing about those features are the sole purview of an Evil Empire, however. <br /> <br /> In its practices, the Scarlet Empire is no more evil than the Roman Empire.<br /> <br /> The last Dynast PC I played was very much a firm believer in the justice of the Realm. She was an agent of the All-Seeing Eye and a devout Immaculate. She saw Solars and Lunars as dangerous anathema who lead mortals astray from the path to Enlightenment and sow discord, disrupting the harmony of the world for their own petty, selfish desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T07:33:51-08:00","id":1365251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1363180#post1363180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly; it states that they're served on platters before rival shahan-yas or their adherents, and that she serves them alive. It seems a bit implicit that the expectation is that such people won't actually do it.<br /> <br /> A chapter fiction depicts her as being coy about somebody relaying the story of her cannibalising enemy soldiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's still made a personal contribution to infanticide, the rest is spliting hairs for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T07:55:54-08:00","id":1365255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1365251#post1365251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She's still made a personal contribution to infanticide, </div> </div> </div> </div>Well, only if any given game group commits to the idea that any Lunar who was presented with such a gesture actually did it. It's hardly infanticide if no children were murdered.<br /> <br /> Focusing again on the context of this being a thing that does not happen often and is targeted at opponents who'll be repulsed by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T08:07:32-08:00","id":1365257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1365251#post1365251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She's still made a personal contribution to infanticide, the rest is spliting hairs for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where it becomes very difficult for me, because a lot of Solar and Lunar characters do very very very bad stuff (because of the Limit Break), so I know they are technically &quot;bad&quot; people in some way, but I think that's also where you have to take a sort of &quot;going forward&quot; morality where you also need to see the morality of a character based on what he intents to do next in his life, not only what he has done (especially when most of them have centuries behind them and will have centuries ahead of them), because else no one is redeemable.<br /> <br /> I'm not advocating infanticide is fine, of course, but I think it's really complicated in Exalted to try and judge a character line Elder lunars and PCs characters. I find it cool that characters in the setting have strong opinions about them because it's thematic, but us discussing of them like the omniscient beings writers and readers about their universe feels a bit off.<br /> <br /> Also the starting point of this specific conversation was &quot;some characters may be a bit alternative to what they are presented as, depending on the ST&quot;. Take the last Maleficient movie for example, I think it's an interesting (simple but still) example of what I was talking about in the first place. That's the point I was trying to make. I'm fine if people don't want Raksi to be changed, I guess this is something that should be talked beforehand, but I also believe these is value in not putting established written characters in stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T14:12:28-08:00","id":1365347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1365251#post1365251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She's still made a personal contribution to infanticide, the rest is spliting hairs for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any moral judgement based solely on a single element of an individual is dangerously reductionist. People are far far more than the worst thing they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T14:16:42-08:00","id":1365349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1365347#post1365347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any moral judgement based solely on a single element of an individual is dangerously reductionist. People are far far more than the worst thing they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I said watching You.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T14:32:13-08:00","id":1365358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1365347#post1365347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any moral judgement based solely on a single element of an individual is dangerously reductionist. People are far far more than the worst thing they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, look back on what Lioness first said about Raksi in this thread.<br /> <br /> Second, that might be technically correct, but it doesn't absolve people of the worst things they do, and there still ought to be lines that function as a point of saying &quot;the other things you do are kind of irrelevant, if not actively thrown into question&quot;. We'll have a problem addressing predators in society of we designate forms of respectability they get to adopt and shield themselves with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1365349#post1365349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I said watching You.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then there's the point where &quot;I'm not entirely the worst things that I do&quot; needs to run up against the point of &quot;there's barely anything else to you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not that the fictional character in question is likely to listen when it displays no indication of really seeing others as actual human beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T15:36:46-08:00","id":1365380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1365358#post1365358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, that might be technically correct, but it doesn't absolve people of the worst things they do, and there still ought to be lines that function as a point of saying &quot;the other things you do are kind of irrelevant, if not actively thrown into question&quot;.<br /> <br /> We'll have a problem addressing predators in society of we designate forms of respectability they get to adopt and shield themselves with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing a bad thing doesn't reverse-absolve people of the best things they do either. There are certainly things so bad that that it's fairly obvious no amount of good can compensate. It's absolutely reasonable to say &quot;You're an OK person, but you'd be a much better person if you stopped doing that one thing.&quot;. It's absolutely reasonable to judge an <i>action</i> as bad, and seek that it not be repeated. <br /> <br /> We'll have a problem addressing people who have corrected their past failings if we designate certain failings as irreversible and refuse to consider their other actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T08:33:06-08:00","id":1365738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1365347#post1365347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any moral judgement based solely on a single element of an individual is dangerously reductionist. People are far far more than the worst thing they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>With a fictional character it's easy to combine &quot;serves up live infants&quot; with &quot;good ruler who cares for their people&quot; Cards Against Humanity style without really exploring the mindset that led to the former character trait existing and how it calls the latter into question.<br /> <br /> Thankfully they didn't do that and gave us a coherent character rather than a morality conundrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T11:17:00-08:00","id":1365770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1365225#post1365225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In its practices, the Scarlet Empire is no more evil than the Roman Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which... was pretty evil.<br /> <br /> But in a nuanced and complex way, which I think the Realm is supposed to be, and I'm happy with its portrayal overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T11:23:43-08:00","id":1365774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1350432-is-you-dynast-pc-evil-or-merely-ignorant?p=1365770#post1365770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which... was pretty evil.<br /> <br /> But in a nuanced and complex way, which I think the Realm is supposed to be, and I'm happy with its portrayal overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also think our notion of evilness comes from a specific spectrum of our time where everything is very static. War of conquest is supposed to be forbidden, we had humanist movement that placed the value of all life sacred and above everything else, we place a huge trust in an universal science that produces solution to a lot of problems from the most mundane to the most complicated, etc ... I like to think the world of Exalted is extremely dynamic and changing than ours, that moral references and culture goes very fast and vary quickly across r\u00e9gions and time, despite The Realm best efforts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:",